s, startup and community engagement, partner activations, and customer advocacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the voice of German customers back to Product, PMM, Marketing, and EMEA leadership, especially around AI transformation, enterprise requirements, security, compliance, localization, and competitive dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a talent destination in Germany by hiring builder-oriented leaders and ICs, raising the craft bar, and developing the next generation of AI-native GTM talent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive operational excellence across forecasting, pipeline quality, territory planning, inspection cadence, performance management, and cross-functional execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1>Who We're Looking For: </h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strategic and hands-on GTM operator who has scaled enterprise SaaS or AI businesses in Germany and knows how to build a market, not just inherit one. You have led through managers, owned complex revenue outcomes, and created local market momentum through customers, partners, community, and talent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine second-line leadership with builder energy. You can set a crisp country strategy, install the operating system to execute it, and step into the field when needed — whether joining an executive customer conversation, sharpening a pipeline plan, coaching a manager, or helping the team translate a customer problem into an AI-powered, agentic workflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are excited by Notion’s shift to an AI-native, country-first GTM model and believe the best GTM teams will increasingly be builders: BDRs who identify transformation opportunities, Solutions Consultants who build with customers in the room, Outcomes Architects who turn early workflows into durable adoption, and Forward Deployed Architects/Engineers who design the technical systems behind complex agentic workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Skills You'll Need to Bring: </h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">12+ years of professional experience, including 5+ years SaaS or AI sales &amp; GTM teams in Germany.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven second-line leadership experience, including hiring, coaching, and developing frontline managers and high-performing IC teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of owning and exceeding revenue targets across new business, expansion, and renewal/churn dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the German enterprise and startup ecosystem, including executive buyer networks, local partner channels, and market-specific buying dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or scaling a regional/country business in a high-growth or ambiguous environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling, implementing, or leading GTM teams around AI, automation, agentic workflows, collaboration, productivity, developer, or data products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong strategic judgment: ability to define a country plan, segment the market, prioritize accounts and plays, and align cross-functional teams around outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational rigor across forecasting, pipeline generation, inspection, performance management, territory planning, and sales process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive presence with CIO, CTO, CPO, COO, and business transformation buyers, with the ability to shape a compelling AI and agentic workflow narrative.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of modern GTM motions across Business Development, Solutions Consulting, Outcomes Architecture, Forward Deployed Architecture/Engineering, Professional Services, Channel, Marketing, RevOps, and Product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Builder mentality and deep AI curiosity: comfortable learning, demoing, and coaching teams on agent-first workflows, proof-of-value motions, and customer co-building.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in German and English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1>Nice to Haves:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience launching or scaling a country-first or regional GTM operating model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with enterprise security, compliance, APIs, webhooks, connectors, data residency, AI governance, and technical evaluation processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience scaling partner, channel, marketplace, or consultant-led GTM motions around AI or workflow transformation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an equal opportunity employer and encourage candidates to apply even if not matching every bullet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is committed to providing highly competitive cash compensation, equity, and benefits. The compensation offered for this role will be based on multiple factors such as location, the role's scope and complexity, and the candidate's experience and expertise, and may vary from the range provided below. The estimated on target earnings (including base salary and on target incentive pay) for this role is €350,000 - 420,000 per year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By clicking “Submit Application”, I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://notion.notion.site/Notion-Global-Recruiting-Privacy-Policy-fc3eb4e829354a26a2bb6fd5e289b550"><u>Global Recruiting Privacy Policy</u></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dev.notion.so/a3ce416456924276a59de91bca740028?pvs=21"><u>.</u></a></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Onsite</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>A Note on AI</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need deep AI expertise for every role, but we do expect every Notino to be intellectually curious, drawn to tinkering and discovery, and excited to use AI as a real collaborator in their work. For some roles, AI fluency is a core requirement — when that’s the case, we'll say so explicitly in the qualifications. People who thrive here don’t treat AI as a novelty. They use it to think better, and make their work easier for others to build on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Equal Opportunity &amp; Accommodations</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire talented people from a wide range of backgrounds. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every bullet, we still encourage you to apply. Notion is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected characteristic. Consistent with applicable law, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. Notion provides reasonable accommodations during the application process; if you need one, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Notion considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Notion is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0;width:100%;height:0;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/0ac11447-a862-468b-95a0-40198c971382/5a7e80f3-d875-4693-938a-33455a593625" style="top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0" allowfullscreen scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/notion/general-manager-dach-munich-445118","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich, Germany","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"account-executive-germany-berlin-212011","company_name":"Wayflyer","title":"Account Executive, Germany","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Wayflyer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today's small businesses need a capital provider that keeps pace with their growth ambitions. Traditional financing options are slow, cumbersome and often out of reach. That's why we built Wayflyer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our technology allows us to assess businesses in minutes, generate financing offers that reflect their growth potential and send funds in as little as 24 hours. To date, we've deployed over $6bn to thousands of businesses worldwide, backed by Tier 1 banks like J.P. Morgan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be collaborating with ambitious colleagues from around the world. We have offices in Dublin, London, New York, Charlotte, Berlin and Sydney.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The challenge</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are thousands of businesses globally growing fast and hitting the same wall - they need capital, and traditional lenders are too slow, too rigid, or simply not interested. We've already deployed over $6bn to growing businesses like these. The opportunity in front of us is significant, and we need people who can capitalise on it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll actually do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the full sales cycle from sourcing your own leads to closing deals with some of the most exciting consumer brands in Germany. You'll run in-depth discovery calls using MEDDPICC, work closely with our underwriting team to move fast without cutting corners, and negotiate deals that genuinely work for both sides. You'll have a dedicated BDR alongside you, but you won't wait around for a full pipeline to land in your lap. The best AEs here source relentlessly, close confidently, and treat their customers like business partners, not transactions. Top performers are hitting ~200% of target. That's not a boast. It's a signal of what’s possible.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What this role could turn into</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Account Executives at Wayflyer tend to grow in one of two directions - first on the ground in one of our emerging verticals, or into team leadership as we scale. We're continuing to launch new products and verticals, which means the people who perform here will have real options. We'd rather promote from within than hire from outside, and our track record reflects that.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who thrives here</strong><br />You've worked a full sales cycle before, and you didn't just hit your number; you understood exactly why you hit it and what to do differently when you didn't. You source your own pipeline without being asked, and you don't wait for perfect conditions to start. You're energised by ambiguity, not paralysed by it. You push deals forward when others would wait for a signal. When a sceptical founder pushes back, you lean in. You've been told "no" and come back with a better question. You care about eCommerce and small business growth, not as a line on a cover letter, but as a genuine reason you want this job.<br /><br /><strong>We hire for range</strong><br />Full sales cycle experience across a range of deal values (think: $10K to 100K) in SaaS or FinTech, ideally with time spent as an outbound BDR/SDR. You know what it takes to build a pipeline from scratch, not just work it. A consistent track record of exceeding targets matters more than tenure. Resilience shows up in your history: you've had a bad quarter, figured out why, and bounced back stronger. MEDDPICC familiarity is required, and you'll need to speak German fluently. Startup or scale-up experience helps; the pace here is real, the playbook is still being written, and we need people who see that as an opportunity, not a risk.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location and working policy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📍</strong>Berlin, hybrid (3-4 days per week in the office)</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The good stuff</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days off, plus public holidays. Equity - because you should own a piece of what you're building. Generous parental leave for primary and secondary caregivers. 60 days a year to work abroad from wherever you want.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Wayflyer Limited will process your personal data for the purpose of evaluating your suitability for the role. Such processing is based on the need to take steps prior to entering into a potential employment agreement. To learn more about how we handle your personal data, you can contact our privacy team at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- or review our privacy notice at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://wayflyer.com/privacy-notice"><em>https://wayflyer.com/privacy-notice</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/wayflyer/account-executive-germany-berlin-212011","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-product-designer-berlin-70645","company_name":"Taktile","title":"Senior Product Designer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Taktile empowers financial institutions to transform into truly AI-native organizations. We’re growing rapidly with enterprise customers across banks and insurance companies, and we’re looking for a Senior Product Designer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building the world's leading software platform for running critical and highly-automated decisions. Our customers use our product to catch fraudsters, prevent money laundering, and expand access to credit for small businesses, among many other use cases. Taktile is making millions of such decisions across the globe every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We do this through a powerful suite of tools that combine ML/AI with heuristics and logic, flexible data integrations, and an overlay of data analytics. We see a high degree of usability as a key differentiator and have been investing in a world-class UI/UX from day one. To help us deliver our vision, we are seeking talented and experienced Senior Product Designers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Product Designer, you will be responsible for translating highly technical and complex problems into clean and understandable solutions. You will be the voice of user experience and design standards in a cross-functional setting, and responsible for the end-to-end design process for your team. You’ll join a diverse design team and work closely with engineers, marketing and sales to create products that make it easy for our users to make smarter and safer decisions at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*Please not that this role is not open to full remote and is Berlin or London based only</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently lead all design efforts for a cross functional team within Taktile.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply design thinking to complex technical problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously learn from user research and be the voice of our customers in product development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct competitive analysis of existing products in the marketplace to identify opportunities for improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect business strategies, available technologies, and design solutions to deliver great experiences that impact our users and our business goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively validate and iterate to ensure our product concepts are aligned with the business needs and stakeholder expectations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with engineers and ensure that designs are implemented effectively in code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to and work with our Design System</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with other designers to create a coherent user experience across Taktile’s product</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in Product Design, ideally with B2B SaaS, fintech, or similarly complex technical domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience leading design for a product area or cross-functional team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong systems thinking and ability to design complex workflows and data-heavy interfaces</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to translate complex technical and business requirements into clear, scalable user experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience driving discovery and shaping problem definitions with Product and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal, But Not Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing agentic interfaces and interest in AI-powered products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical understanding that allows you to engage in discussions with the Engineering Team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in working in a fast-paced start-up/scale-up environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interest in fintech and financial services</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with colleagues that lift you up, challenge you, celebrate you and help you grow. We come from many different backgrounds, but what we have in common is the desire to operate at the very top of our fields. If you are similarly capable, caring, and driven, you'll find yourself at home here.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience a truly flat hierarchy and communicate directly with founding team members. Having an opinion and voicing your ideas is not only welcome but encouraged, especially when they challenge the status quo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn from experienced mentors and achieve tremendous personal and professional growth. Get to know and leverage our network of leading tech investors and advisors around the globe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Receive a top-of-market equity and cash compensation package.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get access to a self-development budget you can use to e.g. attend conferences, buy books or take classes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Receive a new Apple MacBook Pro, as well as meaningful home office set-up.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Stance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're eager to meet talented and driven candidates regardless of whether they tick all the boxes. We're looking for someone who will add to our culture, not just fit within it. We strongly encourage individuals from groups traditionally underestimated and underrepresented in tech to apply</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We seek to actively recognize and combat racism, sexism, ableism and ageism. We embrace and support all gender identities and expressions, and celebrate love in its many forms. We won't inquire about how you identify or if you've experienced discrimination, but if you want to tell your story, we are all ears</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong><br />Taktile enables financial institutions to transform into AI-native organizations that are increasingly powered by autonomous agents. With our modular Agentic Decision Platform, customers combine AI agents, rules, relevant context, and human oversight to safely automate and optimize their decisions—approving more customers, reimbursing claims instantly, stopping fraud before it spreads, and financing every business worth funding. Founded in 2020, Taktile powers millions of decisions daily for institutions including Mercury, Monzo, Faire, and Pleo. With offices in New York, Berlin, London, São Paulo, and Iași, the company has raised $184M from Growth Equity at Goldman Sachs Alternatives, Index Ventures, Tiger Global, Balderton Capital, and Y Combinator. Learn more at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://taktile.com">taktile.com</a></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>About Your Employment.</strong> Taktile operates through regional entities worldwide. Depending on the location of this role, your employment or engagement will be with Taktile LLC (US), Taktile GmbH (Germany), Taktile Ltd (UK), or Taktile SRL (Romania). The applicable entity will be confirmed during the offer process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Your Privacy</strong>. Taktile (“we” or “us”) is the controller of the personal data you provide during this</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>application process. We collect and process your name, contact details, resume/CV, work history, education, and any other information you submit or that we obtain from publicly available sources or references.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>How we use your data</strong>: We process your personal data to evaluate your candidacy, communicate with you about the recruitment process, comply with legal obligations (such as right-to-work verification), and, with your consent, to consider you for future opportunities.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Legal basis (EU/UK applicants):</strong> We rely on (i) pre-contractual steps at your request (GDPR/UK GDPR Art.6(1)(b)), (ii) legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)), and (iii) our legitimate interest in evaluating candidates (Art.6(1)(f)).</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Retention:</strong> If your application is unsuccessful, we retain your data for 12 months after the recruitment process concludes, unless you consent to longer retention. Successful candidates’ data becomes part of their employment records.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Your rights: </strong>Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of your personal data, to data portability, and to withdraw consent.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Automated decision-making:</strong> We use automated tools to assist in screening applications. No hiring decision is made solely by automated means without human review.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>International transfers:</strong> Your data may be transferred to and processed in the United States, Germany, the United Kingdom, or Romania. Where required, transfers are protected by Standard Contractual Clauses or other approved mechanisms.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>By submitting your application, you acknowledge that you have read and understood Taktile’s Applicant Privacy Policy. To exercise your rights or ask questions, contact -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/taktile/senior-product-designer-berlin-70645","tags":["Product & Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin Office","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-integration-specialist-munich-14443","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"(Senior) Integration Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP creates value the moment it is connected to our customers' ERP systems. As an Integration Specialist, you onboard our customers on our integrations and ensure connectivity between BLP and their ERP system. You assess and challenge change requests and specify them for our Integration Engineers. Your work directly drives customer go-lives and revenue. Integration Engineers build, Project Managers lead the project, you make the integration work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboard customers on our ERP integrations: analyze their IT landscape, engage the right stakeholders, advise on best practices, install and configure our ERP integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess and challenge change requests and turn them into a clear, implementable specification for our Integration Engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise customers during self-onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Integration Engineers to continuously improve our integrations and streamline the onboarding experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flag major development needs and blockers early, and make clear recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Project Managers on technical feasibility, effort and sequencing, through first go-live.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in technical consulting, enterprise integration or technical product work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a customer-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid grasp of ERP landscapes, interfaces and master data, and how data actually moves between them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of at least one ERP system (e.g., Microsoft Dynamics, Oracle, Infor, Abas), both from a functional and integration perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with common integration formats (CSV, XML, JSON) and transports (REST/SOAP APIs, SFTP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, spoken and written.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of purchase-to-pay (P2P) and order-to-cash (O2C) processes, including the related finance and accounting workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing specifications that engineers can build from without a translation layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable reading production code, with the help of AI tools, to understand integration behavior and answer customer questions.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real impact: successfully connecting a customer's ERP system decides whether a customer goes live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fast-growing, global AI company providing the ideal environment to learn and grow fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear handoffs: Integration Engineers build and own the product code, Project Managers own the plan, and you own the implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one month of onboarding at our Zurich headquarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership through our stock option program.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/senior-integration-specialist-munich-14443","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-munich-498986","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Senior Project Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time position based in Munich or Cologne. Following a comprehensive onboarding period at our HQ in central Zurich (minimum one month), you will work from your home location, with regular visits to customers across the DACH region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team collaboration matters a lot to us. You will regularly spend time with the team in person, in Zurich and at our hubs, for team days, all-hands and offsites. These visits are financially supported by blp.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get customers live. Hands on, end to end, and fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>As a Senior Project Manager</strong>, you make large, global blp transformations happen. These programs touch finance, procurement and supply chain at once, run across multiple ERP systems and legal entities, and roll out country by country. Your job is to orchestrate all of it and get the customer live: the first go-live above all, because that is where credibility is won or lost, and then wave after wave with the same discipline. You run the steering committee, you lead a blp team on each engagement, and you do that across several engagements at once.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At both levels, scope is the single biggest lever on whether a project goes live on time. Protecting it is a daily job, not a contract clause. You escalate early and precisely rather than absorbing problems until they become critical.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will not be alone with the technical side. Integrations Engineers handle the connection into the ERP, Technical Project Managers handle the harder solution design, and our Consultants take over the automation work after go-live. On our largest strategic accounts a Client Partner carries the relationship and the commercial number, so your attention goes to delivery quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have done this many times, so you are not inventing the approach each time. A proven onboarding method and a strong toolkit are what let you carry your own customers from early on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Career Path in Project Management</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the path most of our delivery leadership came through, and we hire at every step of it. We place you according to your experience and the size of the programs you have delivered, and we are explicit about what the next step requires.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Manager:</strong> You get customers live end to end, several in parallel: guided onboarding for commercial customers, leading enterprise projects yourself, or a workstream on our largest programs. <em>Typically you bring 2+ years in consulting, implementation or project management.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Senior Project Manager:</strong> You make large, global transformations happen: multiple ERPs, entities and countries, the steering committee, and a blp team on each engagement. <em>Typically you bring 5+ years delivering complex, multi-country programs.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Next steps:</strong> Lead a delivery team, or move into Consulting and from there towards our Client Partner role on strategic accounts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moves into Consulting or Customer Success Engineering are open at every level, and many of our people make them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run implementations end to end: kick-off, scope, planning, configuration, testing and go-live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage several customers in parallel at different stages, and keep every one of them on date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with customers on their processes, and flag early where a process assumption will not hold.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate the specialists on your projects: Integrations Engineers, Technical Project Managers and AI Automation Specialists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own scope actively. Recognize a change request for what it is and handle it deliberately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the project inside its budget, and raise it early when the effort is drifting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hand over cleanly at go-live to our Consultants and support organization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In addition, as a Senior Project Manager</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery outcome of global programs from kick-off to the last go-live: plan, scope, dependencies and date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the first go-live relentlessly, then run wave planning across ERPs, entities and countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the steering committee and own the decisions that come out of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and execute the recovery plan when a program is off track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the blp team on each engagement and coach the Project Managers working on your programs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Really Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The following key attributes ensure success in this role:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope Discipline – You notice when a project is quietly growing, and you raise it rather than absorbing it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership &amp; Autonomy – You take initiative, move things forward, and deliver end to end without being chased.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalation Judgment – You escalate early, to the right person, with a proposal rather than a problem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Client Confidence – You are comfortable running a meeting with a customer's finance or IT lead in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Four-Language Fluency – Technology, process, data and people. You speak each well enough to spot where a roadblock really sits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured Under Pressure – When a project goes sideways you get sharper and more organized, not louder.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience delivering complex projects: management consulting, enterprise software implementation, or large-scale transformation delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record running multi-country or multi-entity programs with senior client stakeholders, and steering a committee that includes client executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a delivery team rather than only a plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and communication skills. You can translate a business need into something a technical team can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in German and English, spoken and written.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus points for ERP implementation experience, finance or supply chain processes, or AI-driven SaaS.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership environment – you shape your projects, outcomes, and career path.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact at scale – your work powers automation across global enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-functional exposure – work with engineers, data scientists, and business leaders daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real growth – fast-paced environment, steep learning curve, and structured career progression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership – be part of a majority employee-owned company with a best-in-class stock option program.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Amazing team – become part of a driven and collaborative group of innovators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technology exposure – be at the forefront of AI and enjoy continuous learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visits &amp; offsites – paid visits and stays at our HQ in Zurich, including collaborative team offsites.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to build the future of ERP automation?</strong> Join us and own your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about blp and our values at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blp.digital/company/careers">https://blp.digital/company/careers</a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/compani