></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years in strategy or operations consulting, customer success, professional services or operations leadership, ideally both top-tier consulting and enterprise software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership of organizations of 15+ direct reports, including managing managers, ideally scaled in a fast-growing environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid understanding of purchase-to-pay and order-to-cash and the ERP landscape behind them, for example from finance transformation, shared services or ERP transformations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning commercial outcomes with strategic accounts on executive level such as retention, expansion or cost to serve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive presence: you hold the room with a CFO, especially when the conversation is difficult.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, spoken and written.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in AI-driven enterprise SaaS or in scaling teams across countries is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build an organization: you shape how BLP runs the run phase while it more than doubles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive ownership of our largest and most demanding customer relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaboration with Customer Success leadership, Product, Engineering and Sales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee participation plan</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> We create measurable business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency:</strong> We build trust through openness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> We take responsibility for outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence:</strong> We relentlessly strive for greatness.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/head-of-consulting-munich-293031","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"people-and-business-operations-specialist-hamburg-148664","company_name":"Mindpeak","title":"People and Business Operations Specialist","description":"<h1><strong>Über Mindpeak</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mindpeak ist ein KI-Unternehmen aus Hamburg mit einer klaren Mission: Krebsdiagnosen genauer, effizienter und personalisierter zu machen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wir entwickeln Deep-Learning-Lösungen für die computergestützte Pathologie, die KI direkt in die klinische Praxis bringen. Unsere Technologie wird bereits in mehr als 25 Ländern in der Routinediagnostik eingesetzt und unterstützt führende Pharma- und Biotech-Unternehmen bei der Entwicklung neuer Krebstherapien.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rund 50 Menschen aus Technologie, Medizin und Wissenschaft arbeiten bei uns gemeinsam an diesem Ziel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Über die Rolle</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bei Mindpeak arbeiten wir daran, mit KI die Krebsdiagnostik zu verbessern. Damit sie sich auf ihre Arbeit konzentrieren können, braucht es im Hintergrund jemanden, der dafür sorgt, dass unsere People Operations funktionieren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genau hier kommst du ins Spiel.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als People &amp; Business Operations Specialist bist du das operative Rückgrat unserer People- und Business Operations. Du sorgst dafür, dass neue Kolleg:innen einen guten Start haben, Mitarbeiterdaten stimmen, die Payroll vorbereitet ist, Rechnungen und administrative Finanzprozesse zuverlässig bearbeitet werden, Dokumente rechtzeitig vorliegen, Trainings im Blick bleiben und unsere Mitarbeitenden bei administrativen und organisatorischen Fragen schnell Unterstützung bekommen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR-Administration &amp; Personio:</strong> Du hältst Mitarbeiterdaten, Abwesenheiten, Arbeitszeitmodelle und Dokumente aktuell und sorgst für eine verlässliche Datenbasis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On- &amp; Offboarding:</strong> Du koordinierst die administrativen Schritte rund um Ein- und Austritte, von Google-Accounts und Hardware bis zu Zugängen und Rückgaben, und sorgst für einen reibungslosen Ablauf.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Payroll &amp; Finance Administration:</strong> Du bereitest die monatliche Payroll vor, bearbeitest Rückerstattungen für Mitarbeitende und unterstützt unsere Finanzadministration, insbesondere bei der vorbereitenden Buchhaltung, Rechnungsbearbeitung und Verwaltung von Firmenkreditkarten.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Operations &amp; Prozesskoordination</strong>: Du verwaltest administrative Vertragsfristen, hältst Firmenversicherungen aktuell, koordinierst externe Dienstleister und sorgst dafür, dass wiederkehrende administrative Prozesse strukturiert und zuverlässig ablaufen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR-Dokumente:</strong> Du kümmerst dich um Bescheinigungen, Zeugnisse und weitere administrative Unterlagen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vertragsadministration:</strong> Du bereitest Arbeitsverträge, Vertragsänderungen und Nachträge auf Basis unserer Vorlagen vor und steuerst den Unterschriftenprozess.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sozialversicherung &amp; Benefits:</strong> Du betreust administrative Themen rund um Sozialversicherung, betriebliche Altersvorsorge und Benefits und koordinierst dich mit unseren externen Partnern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance, Trainings &amp; Arbeitssicherheit:</strong> Du administrierst unser Learning Management System, steuerst Pflichttrainings sowie jährliche Unterweisungen zum Arbeits- und Brandschutz  und dokumentierst Trainingsnachweise so, dass sie in Audits (z. B. ISO) belastbar sind.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR-Reporting:</strong> Du erstellst Auswertungen zu Themen wie Headcount, Abwesenheiten oder Trainings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People-Prozesse:</strong> Du unterstützt organisatorisch bei Feedback-Zyklen und anderen wiederkehrenden People-Prozessen und kümmerst dich um Teamrituale wie Geburtstage, Jubiläen und Abschiede.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mitarbeitenden-Support:</strong> Du bist eine verlässliche Anlaufstelle für administrative HR-Fragen und sorgst dafür, dass Anliegen nicht liegen bleiben.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Was wir suchen</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du passt gut zu uns, wenn du:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">eine <strong>abgeschlossene kaufmännische Ausbildung oder eine vergleichbare Qualifikation</strong> mitbringst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">bereits <strong>praktische Erfahrung in Business oder HR-Administration, People Operations oder Personalwesen</strong> gesammelt hast,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">strukturiert, sorgfältig und eigenständig arbeitest und Verantwortung für deine Themen übernimmst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">vertraulich und sorgfältig mit sensiblen Personaldaten umgehst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">auch bei vielen parallelen Aufgaben den Überblick behältst und Dinge zuverlässig zu Ende bringst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">gerne organisierst und Freude daran hast, wenn Prozesse reibungslos funktionieren,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">serviceorientiert bist und gerne dafür sorgst, dass andere gut arbeiten können,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">sicher mit digitalen Tools arbeitest – Erfahrung mit <strong>Personio</strong> ist ein Plus,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">idealerweise schon in einem <strong>regulierten Umfeld</strong> gearbeitet hast, z. B. in MedTech oder einem ISO-zertifizierten Unternehmen (kein Muss),</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">sehr gutes Deutsch und sehr gutes Englisch mitbringst.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Warum diese Rolle wichtig ist</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gute People und Business Operations fallen manchmal erst auf, wenn sie <strong>nicht</strong> funktionieren. Für uns sind sie deshalb kein Nebenthema, sondern eine wichtige Grundlage für ein gut funktionierendes Unternehmen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In dieser Rolle hast du direkten Einfluss auf den Arbeitsalltag unseres gesamten Teams. Du schaffst Struktur, Verlässlichkeit und einen guten Service für unsere Mitarbeitenden – und gibst anderen damit den Rücken frei, sich auf ihre eigentliche Arbeit zu konzentrieren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Was wir bieten</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eine <strong>Rolle mit echter Wirkung </strong>in einem Unternehmen, das mit KI die Krebsdiagnostik verbessert</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ein Remote-Tag pro Woche</strong> – an den übrigen vier Tagen arbeitest du mit dem Team in unserem Büro in Hamburg, mit kurzen Wegen zu allen Kolleginnen und Kollegen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ein wunderschönes Büro mit Blick auf den Hamburger Hafen</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ein tolles, internationales Team</strong> mit kurzen Entscheidungswegen, einer offenen Atmosphäre und gegenseitiger Unterstützung und Wertschätzung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regelmäßige Team-Events</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Guter Kaffee, Müsli und Getränke</strong> – für einen guten Start in den Tag und die kleine Pause zwischendurch</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mindpeak/people-and-business-operations-specialist-hamburg-148664","tags":["General & Administration"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1792226417},{"slug":"sales-intern-dach-market-munich-184333","company_name":"Emidat GmbH","title":"Sales Intern (DACH Market)","description":"<h1>👷🏻‍♀️ What we do 👷🏻‍♀️</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Emidat, we are building the first climate-native product management system for building material manufacturers. We aim to decarbonise building materials, making up 11% of global GHG emissions. We collect data from physical production processes, generate a digital product passport with verified environmental data and make it usable along the value chain. In short: One solution to assess, design, buy, sell and manage products - with environmental impact at the core.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With this, we are building the digital infrastructure to make it faster, easier, and more sustainable to build the world around us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/emidat/Join-Emidat-Enable-a-built-environment-that-operates-within-planetary-boundaries-dbe707b78a8144cb92583ffab4e46c8c"><strong><u>Find out more about us, the team and our values here.</u></strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you will work on</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate Emidat’s growth by acquiring new leads, being Emidat’s first face to the customer and building our predictable, repeatable revenue engine. Work closely with the Sales Development Rep and Account Executive on the go-to-market plan for the country. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our <strong>Sales Intern</strong>, you will be driving our revenue pipeline focussing on the DACH market. In this role, you are the first face and voice to our customer, so this role is perfect if you love being around people and have a talent for convincing, understanding and solving their problems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Emidat, we see top-of-funnel as equally important if not more so than closing deals. Without leads, there is no revenue. We are searching for a hungry sales person, who is not scared of approaching people actively and being the face of Emidat. Your customers are manufacturers, so you shouldn’t be shy and bring a curiosity for material manufacturing and construction <em>(note: we think visiting steel, cement and glass plants is the coolest thing in the world next to customers holding their product into the Teams call to show us how it’s done)</em>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your challenge:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining our sales development team involves:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Pipeline Development:</strong> Build and nurture our customer pipeline, from initial prospecting to booking a demo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go-to-Market Strategy:</strong> Develop and fine-tune our go-to-market strategy, ensuring alignment with our company objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Revenue Engine:</strong> Build and improve our repeatable and predictable revenue engine.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Building</strong>: Play a key role in building and growing the sales team leading us to 3mn ARR.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your first 3 months at Emidat (sample)</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Any Emidavinci starts with a detailed 3-month OKR sheet, which helps to build clarity and accountability from day 1. This is only a high-level overview how this can look like as a Sales Development Executive, but you will find many of the points on your 3-month list in your first week again.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">1. Deeply understand our customer and market</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Mastery:</strong> Call customers, attend conferences and deeply understand our target customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Discovery Calls:</strong> Conduct your first discovery calls and schedule at least 20 demos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Demo Shadowing:</strong> Shadow at least 10 demos to learn how we close deals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">2. Plan and conduct your own outbound campaigns</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Campaign Ownership:</strong> Design your own outbound campaign (incl. list, workflows and sequences). Plan and own 3 campaigns in total</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>RevOps: </strong>Analyze and improve email open/reply rates (target: 25%+ open rate, 5%+ reply rate)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Outbound prospecting:</strong> Execute on the campaigns (e.g. follow-up with calls, send emails/LinkedIn requests)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">3. Get to know and improve our revenue engine design</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CRM / RevOps Mastery:</strong> Become comfortable with our CRM and sales material</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales Playbook &amp; Objection Handling:</strong> Read through our sales playbook, as well as our objection- and competitor handling, start using it and suggest improvements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market understanding:</strong> Understand ICP, persona and JTBD framework; start using it to include your insights</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you will bring to this role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language</strong>: Fluent in German (C2/Native). Proficiency (B2+) in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales Experience:</strong> Demonstrable experience in a business development, growth or sales role. with quantifiable success selling to business customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market Experience:</strong> Experience working with clients / customers in the DACH market in a B2B or B2C capacity. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong Communication Skills:</strong> Effective communication skills, both verbal and written, to communicate with customers and collaborate with team members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> Recently completed or close to completion of a Bachelors Degree in a relevant field (i.e business administration, marketing, sustainability, mechanical / chemical engineering). </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have’s</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language:</strong> Proficiency in another Language relevant to our markets (French, Spanish, Portuguese, Turkish, Italian, Arabic, Hindi).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Startup:</strong> Experience in a start up or scale up environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Industry: </strong>Experience in the construction, material manufacturing or sustainability industries. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education</strong>: Completing or completed a Master Degree in a relevant field. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>How we support you</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your team lead will be</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/elise-lecocq-gj/">Elise Lecocq</a> (Sales Development)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will work with</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/janos-gr%C3%BCndling/">Janos Grundling</a> (Team Lead, Growth)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/joey-quest/">Joey Quest</a> (Sales Development)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/camillo-alemdoust/">Camillo Alemdoust</a> (Account Executive)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/katrina-g-b3990b12a/">Katrina Griese</a> (Sales Development)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/giovanni-michele-genzone/">Giovanni Genzone</a> (Sales Development)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet the rest of the team </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/Join-Emidat-Enable-a-built-environment-that-operates-within-planetary-boundaries-dbe707b78a8144cb92583ffab4e46c8c?pvs=21"><strong>HERE.</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>See our full benefits </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://emidat.notion.site/Benefits-Policies-5bf345ea8cf84c0bac5992bb852f3521"><strong>HERE,</strong></a><strong> including:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💸  Attractive compensation package incl commission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏖️  25 days of vacation days per year (pro rata)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 €500 Learning Budget</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h1><strong>Admin:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date:</strong> As soon as possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role type:</strong> Full-time Internship. Minimum 4 months.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Munich, Germany</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Office Requirement:</strong> Office based</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Travel Required?</strong> Some travel may be required to attend relevant industry events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visa / Relocation:</strong> Preference will be given to candidates already based in Munich and that do not require visa sponsorship. However, we are open to candidates who may need relocation or a visa.</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: €3K – €3.3K per month • €0 – €500 Commission</p><ul><li>Sales Intern Salary • Base Salary €3K – €3.3K per month • €0 – €500 Commission</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/emidat-gmbh/sales-intern-dach-market-munich-184333","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226416},{"slug":"afc-operations-intern-berlin-83578","company_name":"Upvest","title":"AFC Operations Intern (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Upvest, we are on a <strong>mission to make investing as easy as spending money</strong>. Upvest empowers businesses to offer a wide range of investment products and the best experience in the field of capital market investment and retirement planning. Upvest’s Investment API is easy to integrate so that fintechs and financial institutions can save resources and fully focus on their core business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are proud to partner with Europe’s leading Fintechs and financial institutions such as DKB, Revolut, N26 and Raisin. Founded in 2017 by Martin Kassing, Upvest now brings together over 270 talented professionals from more than 70 nationalities. Upvest is backed by <strong>€280M in total funding</strong> from world-class investors, including <strong>BlackRock, Tencent, Sapphire Ventures, and Bessemer Venture Partners, Earlybird, Notion Capital, and Motive</strong>. Our latest <strong>€105M funding round in March 2026</strong> - led by Sapphire and Tencent - serves as a massive catalyst for our growth, allowing us to offer premier investment experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an AFC (Anti-Financial Crime) Operations Intern at Upvest, you’ll be at the forefront of our financial crime defense, playing a hands-on role in safeguarding our platform and our clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll execute Upvest’s first-line-of-defense (1st LoD) AFC processes day to day, the case work that keeps our brokerage infrastructure clean and compliant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time, 6-month internship for someone with a first exposure to AFC / KYC or to the financial sector more broadly, for example through studies, customer support, banking operations, or a previous internship, who is ready to take on a real caseload and grow in autonomy. Depending on performance and business needs, the internship may be extended or converted into a full-time position.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a reliable, detail-oriented person who understands the basics of KYC/AML and is comfortable managing high-volume operational tasks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conducting PEP and Sanctions screening, researching and dispositioning hits as true matches or false positives, with clear, well-documented rationale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performing KYB checks for corporate onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carrying out KYC sample checks, transaction monitoring, and managing the resulting follow-ups with our clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executing and maintaining AFC procedures and controls in line with regulatory requirements and internal policy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Using and helping improve our automation and tooling to make case processing faster and more consistent, for example AI assistants, workflow automation (e.g. n8n), data validation and reporting in the Google Suite (Sheets, Apps Script) and Looker, and basic SQL for querying and cross-checking case data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with the rest of the AFC Ops team and the AML team (2nd LoD) to continuously enhance our AML systems, tools and workflows.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong analytical mindset, exceptional attention to detail, and a genuine interest in compliance and financial-crime prevention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A foundational understanding of KYC/AML concepts, gained through your studies, a previous internship or early work experience in a fintech or financial institution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Early experience in a regulated environment is a plus, but not required.</p>