&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and continuously improve the EMEA RFP and bid management operating framework&lt;/strong&gt;, establishing standardized intake procedures, response workflows, submission controls, and governance practices to ensure consistent and effective execution across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate the end-to-end execution of complex RFP, RFI, and tender responses&lt;/strong&gt;, working closely with Sales, Solutions Engineering, Legal, Compliance, and other relevant functions to obtain required inputs, manage timelines and dependencies, and ensure timely, accurate, and complete submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and continuously improve bid management methodologies and standards&lt;/strong&gt;, identifying operational inefficiencies, evaluating improvement opportunities, and implementing solutions to enhance response quality, turnaround time, and cross-functional effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply specialized knowledge of public and private tender procedures&lt;/strong&gt;, assessing procedural requirements, identifying submission risks, and providing guidance to internal stakeholders on appropriate response processes while escalating matters requiring legal, compliance, or commercial decisions to the relevant functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish and govern a centralized RFP content and knowledge management framework&lt;/strong&gt;, including the administration of Loopio and approved supporting tools, ensuring content accuracy, consistency, currency, and appropriate validation by relevant subject-matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilitate effective cross-functional collaboration throughout the bid response process&lt;/strong&gt;, coordinating contributions from Sales, Solutions Engineering, Product Management, Legal, Compliance, Finance, and Professional Services, and ensuring that dependencies, responsibilities, and escalation requirements are clearly communicated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise independent professional judgment in managing RFP response activities&lt;/strong&gt;, determining when approved content can be used, identifying requirements for additional specialist input, and escalating complex or sensitive matters to the appropriate accountable stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate the review and validation of technical, security, service-related, and contractual information included in bid responses&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring that product capabilities, roadmap statements, security representations, implementation commitments, and service deliverables are reviewed and approved by the relevant authorized functions prior to submission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as the primary operational point of contact for customer procurement representatives and external bid management partners&lt;/strong&gt;, coordinating procedural clarifications, submission requirements, joint-bid activities, and response logistics while involving Sales and other relevant stakeholders in substantive customer discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain RFP management performance reporting&lt;/strong&gt;, monitoring submission volumes, turnaround times, response quality, content effectiveness, and relevant bid outcomes, analyzing operational trends, and recommending process improvements to Revenue Operations and Sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide specialized functional guidance to internal stakeholders on bid management practices&lt;/strong&gt;, supporting the consistent application of established workflows, tender procedures, governance standards, and RFP management tools across the EMEA sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain scalable bid management documentation and implementation playbooks&lt;/strong&gt;, establishing repeatable methodologies and operating practices that support the ongoing development of the EMEA function and potential future adoption in other regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Minimum Qualifications, Education, and Skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:264}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Management, Communications, or a related field, or equivalent relevant professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Knowledge &amp;amp; Job Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in RFP management, proposal management, bid management, or a closely related function, preferably within B2B software or technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience coordinating complex RFPs, RFIs, and tenders involving multiple internal functions and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience establishing, improving, or governing structured bid response processes, including standardized workflows, content management practices, and operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of public and private procurement processes, including open, restricted, negotiated, and competitive dialogue procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying procedural and operational risks and coordinating their resolution with relevant internal subject-matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with RFP management platforms and content repositories; experience with Loopio is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently prioritize RFP activities, manage competing deadlines, and determine when additional specialist input or escalation is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with Sales, technical specialists, Legal, Compliance, and Professional Services in complex bid response environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with B2B software environments; experience in cybersecurity, PKI, or information security is advantageous but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APMP certification or a comparable professional qualification is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Skill&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong bid and proposal project management skills, including planning, prioritization, stakeholder coordination, and deadline management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated process design, documentation, governance, and continuous improvement skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to assess procedural requirements, identify operational risks, and recommend appropriate solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication and content review skills, ensuring accuracy, clarity, and consistency in customer-facing submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional stakeholder management and influencing skills, with the ability to coordinate contributors without direct reporting authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in RFP management tools, structured content repositories, and business productivity applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze operational performance data and translate findings into practical process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple concurrent priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to work effectively across diverse teams and cultures within EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently within broadly defined procedures, policies, and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to apply specialized knowledge and sound professional judgment to complex bid management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish and continuously improve operational processes in a developing functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coordinate multiple stakeholders and manage dependencies while maintaining effective working relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify potential operational, procedural, and submission risks and determine appropriate escalation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence stakeholders through specialized expertise, collaboration, and effective communication rather than formal organizational authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain accuracy, consistency, and attention to detail under competing deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt working methods and priorities to changing business requirements across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to distinguish operational decisions within the role&#39;s authority from matters requiring formal technical, legal, compliance, or commercial approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Travel Requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Up to 15% travel time required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt; color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot;&gt;#LI-NA1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary will be commensurate with experience. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture, Career Opportunities and Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build teams that continually strive to get better than the day before. You will be challenged daily and given opportunities to grow personally and professionally. We balance autonomy and structure to create an entrepreneurial environment to spur creativity and new ideas. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here are just some of the initiatives that make our culture special:  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Second Fridays (a company-wide day off on the second Friday of every month minus November and December due to the Holiday schedule). Please note that this benefit is subject to change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefit coverage globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave is available to new parents. Structure varies based on regional/government requirements. In regions where government-paid leave doesn’t exist, like in the U.S., the company offers generous paid parental leave, along with comprehensive adoption and fertility support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive time off globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedicated employee-focused ambassadors via Key Contributors &amp;amp; Culture Committees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DIVERSE Commitment, a call to action for a more inclusive and diverse future in business, society, and technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Keyfactor Alliance Program to support DEIB efforts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing resources, wellness allowance, mindfulness app free membership, Wellness Wednesdays.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Volunteer Day, company non-profit matching, and 3 volunteer days off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Talent development and Cross Functional meetings to support professional development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular All Hands meetings – followed by group gatherings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Core Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our core values are extremely important to how we run our business and what we look for in every team member:  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is paramount.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We deliver security software and solutions where trust and openness are of the highest importance for our customers. We are honest and a trusted partner in every aspect of business.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; are core.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strategize, operate, and execute through a customer-centric view. We prioritize the security interests of our customers, and we act as if their data were our own.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; never stops, it only accelerates.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The speed of change is accelerating. We are committed, through investment and focus, to stay ahead of the innovation curve.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We deliver with &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;agility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We thrive in high-paced and continually changing environments. We navigate through newly added variables, adjust accordingly, while driving towards our strategic goals.  &lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;United by &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;respect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Respect for all is what unites us. We promote diversity, inclusivity, equity, and acting with empathy and openness, both in our business and in our communities.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; make “it” happen.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vision and goals are not individually achievable – they require teamwork. We pride ourselves in operating as a cohesive team, creating promoters and partners, and winning as one.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keyfactor is a proud equal opportunity employer including but not limited to veterans and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REASONABLE ACCOMMODATION: &lt;/strong&gt;Applicants with disabilities may contact a member of Keyfactor’s People team via ----- and/or telephone at 1.216.785.2990 to request and arrange for accommodations at any time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.keyfactor.com/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;Keyfactor Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/keyfactorinc/senior-rfp-bid-manager-emea-aachen-6546","tags":["Business Transformation"],"job_types":[],"location":"Aachen","created_at":1792216514},{"slug":"engineering-manager-robot-intelligence-munich-433028","company_name":"RobCo","title":"Engineering Manager – Robot Intelligence","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role at RobCo</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">RobCo is building the category of Autonomous Industrial Robotics and we're doing it fast. We believe that automating the ordinary frees humans to do the extraordinary, and we're building the end-to-end robotics infrastructure to make that possible - hardware, software, and AI in one stack that just works. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are now looking for an ambitious <strong>Engineering Manager - Robot Intelligence (m/f/d) </strong>to help us establish RobCo as a leading provider of autonomous automation solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this key role, <strong>you will lead the “brain” of our autonomous robots</strong> - the physical AI harness that works with different models and skills. Managing a full-stack team of software and machine learning engineers, you will balance applied research with business value delivery on a daily basis. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your mission is to translate the latest advancements in physical AI foundation models and complex robotic functionality into a stable, scalable product that thrives in real-world factory environments.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive Engineering Excellence:</strong> Set rigorous standards for code quality, automated testing, and CI/CD pipelines to ensure 24/7 reliability of our robots.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead Senior Talent:</strong> Act as a people-first leader for a team of Senior and Staff engineers, fostering a culture of high ownership and steady delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge Software and Hardware:</strong> Oversee the lifecycle of products spanning from ML training, AI inference to Linux-based industrial interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Balance Research and Delivery:</strong> Establish a strong applied research and experimentation culture, and build a process where the results directly contribute to delivery and practical outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Management Framework:</strong> Work with real-time metrics and steer the team to continuously improve productivity, predictability and quality of what we ship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Governance:</strong> Manage technical debt and architectural health to ensure long-term system stability as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Alignment:</strong> Partner with Product Management to transform customer needs into concrete technical requirements and actionable sprints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Team Leadership:</strong> Mentor junior EMs and help evolve company-wide engineering best practices and software-first principles.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are looking for someone who has:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Completed a university degree in Computer Science, Robotics, Engineering, Data Science or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience leading high-performing teams in complex technical environments like robotics or industrial IoT.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep experience with AI and machine learning, including dataset curation, model training and optimization techniques and hands on experience building agentic harnesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of driving an AI-first engineering culture and implementing agentic workflows that measurably accelerate team velocity and system efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert knowledge in modern SDLC practices, with a track record of improving deployment frequency and system stability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture-aligned mindset characterized by hardware empathy, a passion for software-defined hardware, and a strong culture of high ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience with full-stack software development, robotics engineering is a big plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Very good English skills with the ability to navigate complex architectural discussions with Staff engineers while clearly communicating risks to stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join RobCo?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop modular, software-defined robotics solutions with us that set new standards in automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help us build robots equipped with state-of-the-art AI that perceive their environment, analyze data, and make intelligent decisions in real time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of a very dynamic and fast-growing scale-up, you will take on responsibility from day one, drive your own projects, and see the direct impact of your work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flat hierarchies, open communication, and regular 360° feedback enable fast decisions and support your professional and personal development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wellpass membership (7,200+ studios across Germany), regular team events, and a team that takes both the work and the culture seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours, a modern office, and - depending on the role - the option to work from home.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular team events - from relaxed beer &amp; pizza nights on the rooftop terrace to shared experiences on ski trips or at Oktoberfest.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About RobCo</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Munich in 2020, RobCo leads the transition toward fully Autonomous Industrial Robotics. Our mission is to deploy RobCo in every factory - solving the industrial labor shortage through end-to-end robotics that just works. Powered by Physical AI, our solutions combine a scalable modular hardware architecture with intelligent software that adapts to your use case, improves over time, and requires zero upfront investment through our Robotics-as-a-Service (RaaS) model.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We solve our customers' most pressing pain points - labor shortage, cost pressure, workplace safety, and national reshoring - across the full spectrum of Autonomous Industrial Robotics. With $160M raised from investors including Lightspeed, Lingotto Innovation, and Sequoia, 200+ people globally, and 2.5M+ operating hours in the field, we are deploying robots in factories across Europe and the United States - with our US operations headquartered in Austin, TX, and our RobCo Bay Area Demo Lab in San Francisco.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Don’t meet every single requirement? If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At RobCo, applicants are selected regardless of ethnic origin, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation. All decisions throughout the recruitment process are based solely on applicants’ qualifications, skills, knowledge, and experience, as well as relevant business requirements.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/robco/engineering-manager-robot-intelligence-munich-433028","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792215631},{"slug":"senior-qa-engineer-berlin-153034","company_name":"Resident Advisor","title":"Senior QA Engineer - Berlin","description":"<p><strong>About RA</strong></p><p>Resident Advisor has been a home for electronic music culture since 2001. Event discovery, ticketing, news and long-form editorial, artist profiles, original films, and a weekly mix series two decades deep. Around 7 million people use the web platform every month, with a wider audience across our apps and other channels. Underneath the platform sits a network of contributors and city managers across dozens of cities, which is how we stay connected to the scenes we cover rather than reporting on them from a distance. RA is 25 years old, independent, B.Corp certified and intent on being indispensable to the artists, promoters and audiences who make this culture.</p><p></p><p><strong>Purpose of the role</strong></p><p>As our Senior QA Engineer, you'll look after the quality of <a href="http://ra.co" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">ra.co</a>, our iOS and Android apps, and RA Scan, the app promoters use to scan tickets at the door. You'll work across five product teams. Each team writes and runs its own tests. You'll help them do it well, keep the automated test suites healthy, and test the riskiest releases yourself.</p><p>Some of what we ship carries real risk: payments, checkout, and getting people into venues on the night. Other changes are a line of copy. You'll help us tell the two apart and test each one accordingly. We use AI tools across development, and you'll help the teams use them to write better tests, faster.</p><p></p><p><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the web end-to-end test suite healthy: fix flaky tests, add coverage for new features, and make sure a failing suite gets fixed quickly</li><li>Grow automated testing for our iOS and Android apps and RA Scan with the app developers, so mobile tests run on every change</li><li>Test high-risk releases yourself, such as payments and checkout, including edge cases and what happens when things fail</li><li>Review the test plans teams write, and help them improve</li><li>Use AI tools to write and maintain tests, help developers do the same, and check what the tools produce</li><li>Brief our external testing partner and review the results they send back</li><li>Report bugs clearly, and follow them through with developers and product managers</li><li>Track a few simple measures, such as bugs that reach production and how reliable the automated tests are</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>We’re looking for</strong></p><ul><li>Several years in QA or test engineering, typically four or more, testing web and mobile products</li><li>Hands-on test automation: you've built and maintained automated tests that run in CI, for web (for example Playwright, Cypress or Selenium) and ideally mobile. We use XCUITest on iOS and Espresso with Kotlin on Android</li><li>Enough coding to write and fix tests alongside developers, in a language such as JavaScript, TypeScript, Kotlin or Swift</li><li>You can test APIs and check data with SQL</li><li>Good judgement about risk: what to test deeply, what lightly, and what not at all</li><li>You've used AI tools in your testing work, and know where they help and where they don't</li><li>Clear writing: bug reports and test plans other people can act on</li></ul><p>If you meet most of these but not all, we'd still like to hear from you. Nobody arrives with all of it, and we'll help you grow into the rest.</p><h3></h3><p><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul><li>CircleCI or a similar CI tool</li><li>Working with an external testing partner</li><li>Payments, checkout or ticketing systems</li><li>Testing apps used at live events, with poor networks</li><li>Test management tools such as Qase or TestRail</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What we offer you</strong></p><ul><li>Generous annual leave policies aimed at promoting work-life balance.</li><li>Matched pension, or 401k for US staff.</li><li>Comprehensive staff wellbeing initiatives, featuring regular activities and workplace programmes to support mental and physical health. This includes discounted ClassPass memberships and custom-fitted earplugs.</li><li>Company-led social events, team lunches, and discounts on merch.</li><li>Paid annual volunteering allowance, encouraging contributions to community projects and charities you care about.</li><li>A transparent internal company culture committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion (see: <a href="https://ra.co/about/diversity" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">https://ra.co/about/diversity</a>).</li><li>Active involvement in community projects within the electronic music community (see: <a href="https://ra.co/about/community" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">https://ra.co/about/community</a>).</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>More about RA</strong></p><p>We are independent and we intend to stay that way. 25 years in, RA answers to the culture it came from rather than to outside stakeholders. That is what enables us to make decisions on a long-term basis.</p><p>Our staff, contributors and international teams are not observers. They are part of the scenes we cover, and that is what we hire for. Craft first, and then a genuine stake in this music rather than just a job in it.</p><p>RA has been B Corp certified since 2024, which holds us to standards on social and environmental impact we would want to meet regardless of the badge.</p><p>We especially welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, abilities, ethnicities, experiences, gender identities, and sexual orientations.</p><p></p><p><strong>Our values</strong></p><ul><li>Electronic music is art.</li><li>We celebrate the progressive values that underpin electronic music.</li><li>We advocate for a more inclusive and equitable electronic music community.</li><li>We honour the past, present and future of electronic music.</li><li>We use innovation to empower the community.</li><li>We choose honesty over gain and purpose over profit.</li><li>We're always front left.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Listing details</strong></p><p>This role is a full-time, permanent position, based in Berlin. Please note: this position requires applicants to be based in Berlin and to work from the office three days per week. The annual salary range for this role is €60,000 to €72,000. If you have questions about the role, please contact <a ----- rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" ----- listing will be open for a minimum of two weeks from [date]. Please be sure to add <a ----- rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" ----- to your contacts and check your junk/spam folder for emails from us.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/resident-advisor/senior-qa-engineer-berlin-153034","tags":["Quality Assurance","Music","EPD"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Berlin, Germany","created_at":1792203617},{"slug":"remote-interim-senior-bi-analyst-all-genders-germany-169194","company_name":"Shiftmove","title":"Interim Senior BI Analyst (All Genders)","description":"<p>Across Europe, fleets are under enormous pressure. Fuel costs are rising. Regulatory requirements are tightening. The shift to low-emission vehicles is accelerating. And yet around 70% of European businesses still manage their fleets manually, with spreadsheets, disconnected tools, and processes that were never built for this moment. <strong>Shiftmove</strong> exists to make this simple.</p><p>We are a profitable B2B SaaS company and the fastest-growing fleet management platform in Europe, born from the merger of Avrios and Vimcar, and now serving tens of thousands of corporate customers across Germany, France, Spain, Switzerland, Poland, and beyond. Most recently, we acquired Optimum and Ocean in France, expanding our footprint and doubling down on one of Europe's largest fleet markets. Our AI-powered platform connects real-time vehicle data with intelligent software so that businesses can procure smarter, control costs, stay compliant, and lead the transition to cleaner mobility, all from one place.<br></p><h3><strong>About the role:</strong></h3><p>We are looking for an experienced <strong>Interim</strong> <strong>Senior BI Analyst</strong> to join us on an initial three-month contract, with the option to extend for a further three months.</p><p>As we integrate two acquired French businesses into our group, we need to bring their data into our standard reporting while transforming how our executive team accesses and uses business intelligence. Our existing Tableau dashboards have evolved over time, and we see an opportunity to make them clearer, more consistent and more actionable.</p><p>Reporting to <strong>our VP of Operations, Data &amp; BI</strong>, you will work closely with the executive team, Head of FP&amp;A, RevOps and Data Engineering. You will take ownership of rebuilding our executive reporting, responding to daily analytical requests and ensuring that acquired-company data is accurately reflected in group-wide reporting.</p><p>This is a hands-on role for someone who combines strong technical BI skills with commercial acumen, sound analytical judgement and the confidence to challenge senior stakeholders when the data tells a different story.<br></p><h3> What You'll Do</h3><ul><li><strong>Rebuild ex