&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kirby Group Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kirby Group Engineering is an international multi-disciplinary engineering services contractor and leading provider of high-value engineering services to a number of ‘blue chip’ companies. Operating across Ireland, the UK, Europe and South Africa, Kirby has become the engineering service provider of choice in growth segments such as pharmaceuticals, data centres and power transmission and distribution. Our culture is innovative, collaborative and performance focused. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to grow and develop in a company committed to developing talent and rewarding performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Electrical QC Inspector ensures that electrical systems, components, and installations comply with safety and quality standards. The role includes conducting inspections, testing, and documenting results to verify that work meets project requirements, codes, and industry standards.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Functions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inspection of Electrical Installations:&lt;/strong&gt; Inspect electrical systems and installations during and after the construction process to ensure compliance with safety regulations, project specifications, and industry standards (e.g., NEC, IEC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Control Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor and verify electrical works for quality control, ensuring all installations adhere to engineering drawings, plans, and specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing and Verification:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform a variety of electrical tests (e.g., continuity tests, insulation resistance tests, voltage tests) to verify the functionality and safety of installed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain and complete detailed inspection records, non-conformance reports (NCRs), and testing logs. Provide feedback to supervisors and project managers regarding quality-related issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Conformance&lt;/strong&gt; Handling: Identify and report non-conformance items, working with relevant personnel to resolve issues, ensuring corrective actions are implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with Site Engineers:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with engineers and contractors to resolve quality-related issues and ensure work is executed according to project specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure all electrical work is performed safely, adhering to workplace safety standards and relevant electrical codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inspection of Materials:&lt;/strong&gt; Inspect incoming electrical materials, ensuring that components meet specified standards and quality levels before being used in installations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide feedback and suggestions for improvements in processes, materials, and quality control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Necessary requirement of the Quality Control Inspector:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong Trade/Construction background and/or a third level qualification in Electrical/Mechanical Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 3 year’s experience in a lead/managerial position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and people skills with the ability to adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on own initiative is essential as well as taking direction where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in conjunction with others and be a team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to working to the highest possible standards and delivering high quality results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in the use of MS office, BIM 360 Field Management or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Centre, Pharma or similar experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired competencies / special roles requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Electrical Testing &amp;amp; Commissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CompEx Ex01-04 training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of working on HV/MV systems. ‘Authorised person’ experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on this or opportunities based in Ireland, UK or Europe contact the&amp;nbsp;Talent Acquisition Team in Kirby Group confidentially on&amp;nbsp;+353 (0)1 454 0411 or apply in confidence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on this role, or other Construction / Engineering opportunities across Ireland, the UK, Europe, or South Africa please review our careers page (&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.kirbygroup.com/vacancies/&quot;&gt;Vacancies - Kirby Group Careers&lt;/a&gt;) or contact the Talent Acquisition Team at Kirby Group in confidence on +353 (0)1 454 0411.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kirby Group Engineering is an equal opportunities employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates, regardless of race, gender, disability, religion, sexual orientation, or age.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/kirbygroupengineering/qc-inspector-germany-326632","tags":["Quality Control K220"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792194924},{"slug":"senior-influence-manager-berlin-dusseldorf-369304","company_name":"Ogilvy","title":"Senior Influence Manager (m/w/d)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ogilvy &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy has been creating impact for brands through iconic, culture-changing, value-driving ideas since the company was founded by David Ogilvy more than 75 years ago. It builds on that rich legacy through Borderless Creativity—innovating at the intersection of intelligence, imagination and influence, with experts across advertising, sports &amp;amp; entertainment, PR &amp;amp; social, consulting, and health collaborating seamlessly across more than 120 offices spanning 90 countries. Ogilvy was named &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-brings-home-network-year-2026-cannes-lions-international-festival-creativity&quot;&gt;Network of the Year&lt;/a&gt; at the 2026 Cannes Lions International Festival of Creativity and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-tops-warc-effective-100-creative-100-4th-straight-year&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;e2c78315-ff05-4544-925f-9288319dea2c&quot;&gt;ranks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;as the #1 global agency network for creative excellence and effectiveness by WARC for the fourth consecutive year, signifying its ability to deliver creative solutions that drive unreasonable impact for clients and communities. Ogilvy is part of WPP, the trusted growth partner for the world&#39;s leading brands. Powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform WPP Open, WPP unites cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, creativity, production, enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ogilvy.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;39833259-880d-4fd8-930f-0d84b1c14850&quot;&gt;Ogilvy.com&lt;/a&gt;, and follow us on&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;735e393e-6e8a-4ca8-804a-74f1bd8166b6&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ogilvy&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d10960ce-761b-48c5-81d5-0a7c4cc6013a&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;92ffcb70-6ca7-4d9a-88d5-c130e36e6c4f&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;3bd2010d-00a2-401b-8cfb-7e8c24deac52&quot;&gt; Facebook.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&amp;nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&amp;nbsp;in a single company –&amp;nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&amp;nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://wpp.com/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;7f087527-f491-4cb6-a79d-3b4a67d1ec89&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;column&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Du hast Lust strategische Influencer-Kampagnen zu entwickeln und umzusetzen und möchtest mehr „Purpose“ mit deiner Arbeit bewirken, indem du Marken und Unternehmen strategisch mit gesellschaftlich relevanten Themen verknüpfst? Dann bist du bei uns genau richtig: „We inspire brands and people to impact the world“ – Ogilvys Vision ist es, Marken und Menschen dafür zu begeistern, die Welt zu verändern. Diese Vision treibt auch uns bei Ogilvy Public Relations an.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unsere Kommunikations-Allrounder beraten Kunden in den Bereichen Corporate, BtC und BtB Communications sowie Social Media, Influencer und Content Marketing. Was uns ausmacht: Tiefe Marken-&amp;nbsp;und Unternehmenskenntnisse, Leidenschaft für kreative Kommunikation und die Maxime “We, not me”.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zum nächstmöglichen Zeitpunkt suchen wir also &lt;strong&gt;eine:n &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Senior Influence Manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;(m/w/d) &lt;/strong&gt;in Düsseldorf oder Berlin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Das bieten wir: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Möglichkeit zur Arbeit im Mobile Office (drei Präsenztage vor Ort)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nutzung unseres&amp;nbsp;WPP Weiterbildungsnetzwerkes, inkl. LinkedIn Learning&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unterstützung bei der privaten Altersvorsorge und die Gewährung von vermögenswirksamen Leistungen&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jubiläumsprämien in Form von zusätzlichen Urlaubstagen&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Möglichkeit zur Nutzung eines Job Bikes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erweiterte Betriebliche Krankenversicherung mit einem zusätzlichen Budget von bis zu 300€ im Jahr&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zugriff auf unser&amp;nbsp;Employee&amp;nbsp;Assistance Programm&amp;nbsp;TELUS Health&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kostenlose Nutzung der&amp;nbsp;Headspace-App&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subventionierte&amp;nbsp;Gympass-Mitgliedschaft&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deine Aufgaben:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operative Steuerung unserer Influencer-Kampagnen, von der Konzeption und Umsetzung bis hin zur Überwachung und dem Projektcontrolling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entwicklung von Influencer-Strategien inklusive der Empfehlung von Zielsetzungen, Zielgruppen, Redaktionskalendern und Budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du entwickelst Strategien nicht nur, sondern setzt sie auch eigenverantwortlich und operativ selbst um – von der Konzeption bis zur täglichen Kampagnensteuerung.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recherche, Aufbereitung, Präsentation und Ansprache relevanter Influencer für die Kampagnen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budgetcontrolling der Influencer-Kampagnen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Abstimmung und Zusammenarbeit mit allen relevanten Stakeholdern - intern und extern - um für unsere Kund:innen passende Kampagnen zu entwickeln und umzusetzen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weiterentwicklung und Verwaltung unserer Influencer-Datenbank&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kundenbindung und -zufriedenheit sowie Qualitätssicherung der Agenturleistungen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Auswertung, Analyse und Reporting von Influencer-Kampagnen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Was du mitbringst:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bist ein Talent, möchtest den Quereinstieg wagen und hast anschauliche Beispiele uns das zu präsentieren oder du hast 3-5 Jahre Berufserfahrung im Influencer Marketing und kennst dich bestens in der deutschen Creator Szene aus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ausgewiesene Erfahrung in den Bereichen Konzeption, Kampagnenplanung und -durchführung, Influencer Relations, Events, Social Media und Projektmanagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Umfassende Kenntnisse und Kontakte im Bereich Influencer Relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du hast eine hohe Affinität für aktuelle Trends und bist am Puls der Zeit bei cultural und social Themen.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Präsentationsstärke: Fähigkeit, kreative Ideen vor internen Stakeholdern sowie bestehenden und potenziellen Neukunden sicher zu präsentieren&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bist Teamplayer, besitzt eine hohe Kundenorientierung und Qualitätsanspruch sind für dich selbstverständlich&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sehr gute MS-Office-Kenntnisse sowie gute Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrungen mit Influencer Recherche- und Analyse-Tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wir glauben an die Kraft von Diversität und Kollaboration. Den Herausforderungen der heutigen Welt können wir nur gemeinsam begegnen. Wir verpflichten uns daher, für den Job in Frage kommende Bewerber:innen ausschließlich nach ihren Fähigkeiten und grundsätzlich unabhängig von Alter, Geschlecht, ethnischer Zugehörigkeit, sexueller Orientierung, Behinderung oder Religion zu beurteilen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Das klingt nach einer spannenden Herausforderung? Sehr gut, dein Ansprechpartner Kai Schlüter&amp;nbsp;freut sich über deine Bewerbung!&lt;br&gt;Aus Gründen der Nachhaltigkeit und des Datenschutzes bitten wir darum, Bewerbungsunterlagen ausschließlich über unsere Bewerber:innenplattform Greenhouse an uns zu senden. Wir würden uns freuen, wenn auf das Mitsenden eines Fotos verzichtet würde.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ogilvy, our people are at the heart of what we do: a creative agency that sparks game-changing ideas across culture and business through collaboration, integrity, and a celebration of self-expression.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in building powerful teams with purpose - and we relentlessly curate transformative initiatives that make our commitment to fairness, and equity a reality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ultimate mission is to leave a positive impact on the world, creating a better future for all, while supporting and uplifting the global communities we serve.&amp;nbsp; This is central to our mantra of Borderless Creativity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ogilvy is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any assistance seeking a job opportunity, or if you need reasonable accommodation with the application process, please contact us at ----- Please note that this contact is only for candidates who are requesting accommodation. Emails for other purposes, including application status requests, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/ogilvy/senior-influence-manager-berlin-dusseldorf-369304","tags":["Public Relations"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin; Düsseldorf","created_at":1792194924},{"slug":"staff-forward-deployed-engineer-ai-native-software-development-berlin-munich-273313","company_name":"jetbrains","title":"Staff Forward Deployed Engineer – AI-Native Software Development","description":"&lt;p&gt;At JetBrains, code is our passion. Ever since we started, back in 2000, we have strived to make the strongest, most effective developer tools on earth. By automating routine checks and corrections, our tools speed up production, freeing developers to grow, discover, and create.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We just unveiled JetBrains Central,&amp;nbsp; a platform for agent-driven software development that connects tools, agents, and infrastructure. It enables automated AI workflows to run, be monitored, and be managed across teams – with clear visibility into results, costs, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JetBrains Central provides three core capabilities:&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance and control: &lt;/strong&gt;Policy enforcement, identity and access management, observability, auditability, and cost attribution for agent-driven work. Some of these functionalities are already available via the &lt;a href=&quot;http://console.jetbrains.cloud/&quot;&gt;JetBrains Central Console&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent execution infrastructure:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Cloud agent runtimes and computation provisioning that allow agents to run reliably across development environments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent optimization and context:&lt;/strong&gt; Shared semantic context across repositories and projects, enabling agents to access relevant knowledge, and task routing to the most appropriate models or tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inside the Professional Services department, we are building a team of Forward Deployed Engineers to help our customers adopt AI-native development with JetBrains Central and enable JetBrains consulting partners to transform their customers’ AI-native software development lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Forward Deployed Engineer, you will work directly with early adopter customers to deploy JetBrains Central platform into complex enterprise environments and help them move from experimental AI usage to governed, scalable AI-native development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted advisor to customer engineering teams and consulting partners, while also mentoring other Forward Deployed Engineers and helping with complex deployments. In this role, you will help establish best practices for enterprise AI adoption and influence how organizations implement AI-driven software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is often a strong fit for engineers who have previously served as Principal or Staff Engineers, Heads of Engineering, CTOs, or Solutions Architects and who enjoy working directly with customers while staying deeply involved with complex technical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines consulting, architecture, and hands-on engineering. Your work in the field will directly influence how our platform evolves and how enterprises adopt AI-driven development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the world’s most innovative companies — our client base includes 420 of the Fortune 500 — ensuring they maximize the value of their JetBrains investments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy JetBrains Central platform into enterprise development environments, CI/CD systems, and internal developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help organizations transition from ad-hoc AI experimentation to governed AI-native development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement enterprise AI governance, including security policies, access management, and data privacy controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable observability for AI-driven development to help organizations understand their AI usage and its impact on productivity, as well as their code-generation patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design sustainable AI adoption strategies, including usage controls and cost visibility across multiple model providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate our cloud-based agent execution layer, allowing AI agents to run securely and at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with JetBrains product teams to shape the platform based on real-world deployments and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create delivery frameworks and train JetBrains partners to deliver the desired scope of service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support other Forward Deployed Engineers, sharing architectural expertise and helping to scale the team’s deployment practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in this role if you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultant at heart who can communicate effectively with both engineers and technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to see the whole picture of the software development lifecycle across developer tools, infrastructure, APIs, and cloud systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced at integrating complex software systems into enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about the future of AI agents and AI-native software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with early adopters and overcoming ambiguous technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated to mentor other engineers and contribute to building a new technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in software-related projects, ideally in a customer-facing or consulting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Java or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or integrating developer platforms, infrastructure systems, or software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern development workflows (CI/CD, developer environments, internal developer platforms, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers or technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to operate in fast-evolving technical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and desire to travel to meet customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;These would be a plus, but are not blockers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industry-specific solutions (fintech, telco, retail, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI/LLM platforms, agent frameworks, or AI-assisted development tools.&lt;br&gt;Experience in solutions engineering, consulting, or forward-deployed engineering roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the JetBrains ecosystem or developer productivity tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-KP1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We process the data provided in your job application in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/privacy/privacy-recruitment/&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/jetbrains/staff-forward-deployed-engineer-ai-native-software-development-berlin-munich-273313","tags":["Professional Services"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin; Munich","created_at":1792194921},{"slug":"senior-web-ux-ui-designer-berlin-munich-316297","company_name":"jetbrains","title":"Senior Web UX/UI Designer","description":"&lt;p&gt;Do you care deeply about visual hierarchy, interaction details, and how a webpage feels to use? Do you believe design isn’t decoration, it’s how products communicate, guide, and solve complex problems? If you enjoy refining pixels, building coherent web systems, and eliminating friction for smart users, this is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JetBrains&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create intelligent software development tools for developers and teams. More than 15 million users, over 300,000 companies, and 88 of the Fortune Global Top 100 rely on our products to solve real, complex problems. Our mission is simple: make development teams more productive and AI adoptable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our web presence is often the first interaction developers and teams have with JetBrains. As software evolves, our web products and tools need to clearly communicate complex concepts while staying intuitive, accessible, and fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take ownership of major web design initiatives across our ecosystem. Instead of applying surface polish, you’ll tackle core visual and structural challenges, building scalable design patterns, improving user journeys, and shaping how our web interfaces operate across devices. You’ll collaborate directly with product managers and developers, bringing visual clarity to complicated workflows and ensuring our web pages meet the high standards our users expect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design responsive, accessible web pages and interaction flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and evolve scalable web design systems and UI component libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex technical concepts and user requirements into intuitive visual experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with developers to ensure implementation stays true to design intent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test, iterate, and refine designs based on user feedback and real-world usage patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to structure, layout systems, and interaction details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems-thinking mindset that prioritizes consistency and scalability over isolated fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, articulate reasoning behind design decisions when collaborating with other teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong self-direction and comfort taking ownership of end-to-end design initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine curiosity about how users interact with web pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating complex Web/UI/UX projects delivered from concept to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with modern design and prototyping tools like Figma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of modern web standards and responsive design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and managing web design systems and UI component libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing accessible, inclusive web interfaces aligned with WCAG standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success means delivering web experiences that feel effortless, consistent, and visually refined. You’ll know you’re succeeding when complex user flows become clear, design components scale seamlessly across products, and both internal teams and end-users trust the quality of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join JetBrains?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong base salary. We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work location. Enjoy the freedom to work from home or from the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote work. Spend up to 30 days per year working remotely from abroad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra time off. More days to relax, recharge, and do the things you love.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical insurance allowance. Enjoy peace of mind for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities. Access to conferences, courses, and language classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language classes. Pick up the local language or sharpen your English skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fuel your day. Enjoy a hot meal or receive a lunch allowance on workdays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health support. To help you feel your best, we provide easy access to professional mental health services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sports benefit. Enjoy an on-site gym or sports club stipend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal events. Join company-wide celebrations and team gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Some benefits may vary depending on location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like you, send us your portfolio and tell us about work you’re proud of.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-DNI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We process the data provided in your job application in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/privacy/privacy-recruitment/&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/jetbrains/senior-web-ux-ui-designer-berlin-munich-316297","tags":["Web Design"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin; Munich","created_at":1792194921},{"slug":"it-program-manager-berlin-71517","company_name":"Moss","title":"IT Program Manager (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Moss, we give finance professionals the power to automate their day-to-day and make forward-thinking decisions.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our culture is what makes that possible: we play to win, we obsess over quality, and we win as One Moss, and it works. Moss closed a €35 million Series C in August 2026, crossing a €1 billion valuation, and became one of Europe's fintech unicorns. Join us for what's next.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring an IT Program Manager who will be at the centre of how Moss buys, manages and eventually retires technology. You'll own the vendor and contract landscape, steer the Tech Operations budget, and lead the company-wide platform migrations and consolidations that come a few times a year. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll report to the CISO and work closely with our Tech Operations engineers and Information Security team, alongside Legal, People Ops and FP&amp;A, across a technology estate spanning 350 people and five offices.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own vendor and contract negotiations across Moss's SaaS, tooling, infrastructure and connectivity providers, running competitive evaluations to build commercial leverage and maintaining the renewal calendar and contract repository</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and steer the Tech Operations budget, creating cost transparency per team and driving licence right-sizing, optimisation and consolidation across the tool estate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with teams across Moss to understand how tools are actually used, matching licence tiers to real usage and deciding which overlapping tools to keep based on what genuinely serves people, not just cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive down the number of tools Moss runs by finding shadow IT, bringing it into the process or consolidating it, and owning retirement work together with Information Security</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead company-wide technology migrations and retirements end to end, from business case and migration plan through cutover, communication and training</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring structure to how work reaches Tech Operations, building a clear intake process and owning the KPIs and monthly management reporting for the domain</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Legal on contracts and DPAs and with People Ops on joiners and leavers, owning the commercial relationship and negotiation for the vendors in your portfolio within Moss's existing Vendor Management framework</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of experience in IT vendor management, procurement, sourcing, tech operations or IT service management, ideally gained in a scaling company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience negotiating with vendors and providers, including on service levels and cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading at least one company-wide tool migration or consolidation end to end, including decommissioning the old system</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on IT background, enough to keep essential services running from documented runbooks in an emergency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is core to how we work. We expect someone with an "AI Driver" toolkit: measurable, real-workflow AI use with concrete before/after impact, ideally including built automations or agents (n8n, Claude skills, or similar).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German at C1 or above, prior experience in a regulated environment (financial services, payments or e-money), exposure to ISO 27001, SOC 2 or DORA, or an ITIL/IAITAM qualification are all a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition, here are the skills and attributes we are looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A talent for moving things forward through clarity and good process rather than hierarchy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable owning commercial outcomes inside a governance framework someone else owns</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine curiosity about how other teams work, and translating that into better commercial calls than a dashboard would</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, documentation-friendly way of working, with an instinct for turning manual work into something that runs itself</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Moss</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moss is the Finance AI platform for Europe's mid-sized businesses, giving companies real-time visibility and full control over their spend. By automating card issuing, invoice management and expenses, Moss simplifies financial workflows and frees finance and accounting teams from manual, administrative work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Berlin and used by more than 10,000 businesses including Flink, Schufa, n8n and Auto1, Moss has raised €220+ million to date and operates in Germany, the Netherlands, the UK and further EU markets. In August 2026, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getmoss.com/magazine/moss-series-c?origin-page=en-us%2Fcareers"><u>Moss closed a €35 million Series C </u></a>led by Portage, crossing a €1 billion valuation and becoming one of Europe's newest fintech unicorns. Moss is backed by investors including Valar Ventures, Tiger Global, Global Founders Capital, Cherry Ventures, A-Star.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a team of 300+ people from 50+ nationalities across 5 offices in Europe and we hire, reward, and grow people based on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/moss-finance/life/c2ac8184-5388-4962-ad07-e0bcbfe080f0/?viewAsMember=true"><u>Moss DNA</u></a>: playing to win, obsessing over quality, winning as One Moss. If that's how you want to work, we want to hear from you. - here's <strong>what else to expect:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top-of-market compensation package, including equity. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our vibrant offices are at the heart of our culture, where in-person time fuels collaboration and connection over weekly breakfasts and Friday demos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional benefits include: 20 days “work from abroad”, 600EUR/GBP Learning &amp; Development Budget, and other local benefits.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Unless stated otherwise, benefits apply to full-time positions (interns and working students receive a tailored package).</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>By applying for the above position, you will confirm that you have reviewed and agreed to our </strong></em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getmoss.com/privacy-policy"><em><strong><u>Data Privacy Policy</u></strong></em></a><em><strong>.</strong></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/moss/it-program-manager-berlin-71517","tags":["Operations & Risk"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792194022},{"slug":"projektmanager-photovoltaik-berlin-270743","company_name":"GALVANY","title":"Projektmanager Photovoltaik (m/w/d)","description":"<h2>Projektmanager Photovoltaik (m/w/d)</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bei GALVANY ist es unser Ziel, klimaneutrales Wohnen für alle zur Realität zu machen. Wir setzen auf Umsetzung und entwickeln konkrete, smarte Lösungen, indem wir Wärmepumpen, Batteriespeicher und Smart Metering einfach zugänglich, zuverlässig und bezahlbar machen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wir sind ein profitables Greentech-Startup und glauben, dass nachhaltiger Impact und langfristiges Wachstum nur auf Basis eines gesunden Geschäftsmodells möglich sind. Um unsere ambitionierte Tech Roadmap umzusetzen haben wir im Frühjahr 2026 eine Seed-Finanzierung in Höhe von 10 Millionen Euro mit Set Ventures und AENU abgeschlossen. Getrieben von Kundennutzen, Klarheit und Verantwortung stehen wir für hochwertige Heizlösungen und ein Arbeitsumfeld, in dem Menschen Verantwortung übernehmen und nachhaltigen Mehrwert schaffen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als Projektmanager Photovoltaik (m/w/d) verantwortest du die operative Steuerung unserer PV-Projekte von der Vertragsunterschrift bis zur fertigen Installation auf dem Dach. Du bringst unsere Kund:innen strukturiert, effizient und profitabel durch die gesamte Projektphase und koordinierst dabei eng mit unseren Lieferanten und Installationsbetrieben. Du arbeitest KPI-getrieben, greifst proaktiv ein und lässt kein Projekt liegen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du steuerst PV-Projekte aktiv von Unterschrift bis Abschluss mit dem Ziel, die Cycle Time konsequent zu reduzieren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du koordinierst den direkten, operativen Draht zu PV-Modul-Herstellern, Großhändlern und Installationsbetrieben und sorgst für reibungslose Abstimmung bei Beschaffung, Terminierung und Durchführung.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du greifst proaktiv ein, sobald Zeit-KPIs überschritten werden oder Risiken für Durchlaufzeit, Profitabilität oder Kundenzufriedenheit entstehen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du gewährleistest, dass Projekte vollständig, baubar und jederzeit korrekt im System abgebildet sind und kein Projekt verloren geht.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du behältst die Vollständigkeit der Projektunterlagen im Blick – erkennst frühzeitig, was fehlt, und sorgst dafür, dass es rechtzeitig vorliegt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast die Profitabilität pro Projekt im Griff: Engpässe und Wartezeiten identifizierst du rechtzeitig, bevor sie auf das Ergebnis drücken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du arbeitest eng mit dem Customer Support Team zusammen und übernimmst die proaktive, projektspezifische Kommunikation zu definierten Kontaktpunkten.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du schaffst transparente und aktuelle Projektstatus und gibst jederzeit Klarheit über Blocker und Handlungsbedarf.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du baust die Prozesse für PV-Projekte aktiv mit auf und entwickelst sie kontinuierlich weiter, da es sie bei uns in dieser Form noch nicht gibt.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dein Profil</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Abgeschlossene Berufsausbildung oder Studium in einem relevanten Bereich (z. B. Technik, Handwerk, Energie, Wirtschaft) oder vergleichbare Praxiserfahrung im Projekt- oder Operationsumfeld.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung im Projektmanagement, in Operations oder in einem technischen Umfeld (z. B. Bau, Handwerk, Energie).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Verhandlungssicheres Deutsch in Wort und Schrift (C2).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sicherer Umgang mit CRM-Systemen und digitalen Tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung im Umfeld Photovoltaik, Wärmepumpe oder erneuerbare Energien ist ein Plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zusätzlich sind uns folgende Fähigkeiten und Eigenschaften wichtig:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership</strong> – Wenn ein Projekt ins Stocken gerät, hast du das Problem längst erkannt – und bereits gehandelt. Du treibst Projekte intern konsequent voran, adressierst Abhängigkeiten klar und verbindlich gegenüber anderen Teams, und bleibst so lange dran bis das Ergebnis steht.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expert Operator</strong> – Du hast viele Projekte gleichzeitig im Blick – und weißt bei jedem, wo es steht, was als nächstes passieren muss und wo Gefahr droht. Prozesse und Prioritäten sind deine Werkzeuge, um auch bei hohem Volumen handlungsfähig zu bleiben.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-Driven Optimizer</strong> – Cycle Time, Profitabilität, Terminierungen &amp; Projektfortschritt – du schaust täglich auf deine KPIs, erkennst Muster bevor sie zum Problem werden und nutzt diese Erkenntnisse, um deinen Prozess kontinuierlich zu schärfen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercially Minded</strong> – Du weißt, dass Verzögerungen nicht nur Kunden frustrieren – sie fressen direkt in die Profitabilität. Du erkennst frühzeitig, wenn Wartezeiten oder Eskalationen auf das Ergebnis drücken, und steuerst aktiv dagegen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proactive Problem Solver</strong> – Fehlende Unterlagen, blockierter Installationstermin, unerreichbarer Kunde – du lässt dich davon nicht aufhalten. Du findest einen Weg und sorgst dafür, dass das Projekt weiterläuft.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Werde Teil eines schnell wachsenden und profitablen Climate-Tech-Startups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attraktive und wettbewerbsfähige Vergütung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unser lebendiges Office ist das Herz unserer Kultur und fördert Zusammenarbeit und Austausch vor Ort</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrides Arbeitsmodell mit anteiligem Homeoffice nach der Einarbeitung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individuelle Benefits, abgestimmt auf deine Bedürfnisse, z. B. Sportmitgliedschaften, ÖPNV-Ticket oder Learning Budget</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/galvany/projektmanager-photovoltaik-berlin-270743","tags":["CEO Office"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792194022},{"slug":"senior-sales-executive-dach-berlin-184651","company_name":"Siteminder","title":"Senior Sales Executive, DACH","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At SiteMinder, we believe our success comes from our people. We build diverse, inclusive teams where different voices, backgrounds and perspectives are valued. Our differences drive innovation for our customers, and our people bring the ideas, expertise and energy that help us keep moving forward. We’re better together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we do...</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Right now, somewhere in the world, a hotel is taking a booking or increasing their revenue through technology you could help build. SiteMinder is the world’s leading hotel commerce platform. For more than 20 years, we’ve helped hotels attract guests, maximise revenue, forecast demand and perform at their best. Today, our platform supports 56,000+ hotels in 150+ countries, connects to 3,000+ partners and powers more than 140m reservations and AU$85 billion+ in hotel revenue each year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That’s the kind of impact your work can have here. You’ll solve meaningful challenges with AI, simplify complexity and build solutions that help hotels perform. Supported by clear purpose, a strong platform and teams who care about what they’re building, you’ll have the opportunity to shape the future of an industry that never stands still.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Senior Sales Executive role...</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your SaaS Sales career? Do you want to be part of the technology shaping the future of the travel industry? Join our international, dynamic and outgoing team in Barcelona!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will become a trusted advisor to hotel owners, building awareness about how our products can benefit their property. You will have the chance to learn about the challenges that accommodation providers face, and offer a solution that will bring value to their day-to-day and bottom line. Joining SiteMinder as the leader in dynamic hotel revenue management, you will be at the forefront of innovation in the sector. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We won't throw you into the deep end - you'll be trained on our products, industry and sales processes. We have a month-long sales training and onboarding program to make sure you are set up for success. You will be supported by a dedicated sales coach and a buddy, as well as your team leader, who will coach and motivate you to achieve your professional goals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that an attractive compensation package is a key motivator in sales. SiteMinder offers you not only this, but also a working environment that represents ambition, collaboration, self-development and customer-centricity. If you identify with our core values (We Hustle, We Come Together, We Grow, We Make Things Simple) and you are a sales hunter at heart, we want to hear from you!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do...</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Client acquisition</strong> - Create new opportunities and upsell current customers. You will be responsible for the full sales cycle, from outreach to demo and closing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Achieving sales KPIs and targets</strong> - Working towards daily, weekly and monthly targets and finalize all sales in a timely manner. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Presentation and negotiation</strong> – Prepare accurate quotes and develop and present proposals to clients in a professional and confident manner. Negotiate contracts as required, maintaining a balance between optimal service and value for the client and SiteMinder's profit margins. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CRM maintenance </strong>– Maintain accurate records of your business development activities on SiteMinder's CRM system.  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Client feedback</strong> – Provide client feedback on products to the Product Team so that products can be reviewed in line with the feedback. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner management</strong> – Work with local industry groups and travel associations to promote SiteMinder’s products and brand. Attend key functions and events, requiring occasional travel to client locations to attend meetings with relevant managers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you have...</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) sales</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent in German (min. C2) </strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional proficiency in English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A confident phone presence, fearlessness in leading meetings with prospects, and great listening skills </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills professionally with customers, in writing and over the phone </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivation and resilience to show up each day and give your best </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth mindset - openness to feedback and coaching</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Please send us your CV in English!</em></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Perks &amp; Benefits…</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote setup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity packages for you to share in SiteMinder's growth and successes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investment in your personal growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Uncapped commission that rewards overachievement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellence-driven, collaborative culture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Well-being initiatives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Referral bonus for bringing in new talent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous parental (including secondary) leave policy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid birthday, study and volunteering days off every year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee Resource Groups (ERG) to help you connect and get involved</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Think this role sounds like you? If so, we’d love to hear from you. Please send us your resume and our Talent Acquisition team will be in touch.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">When you apply, feel free to share your pronouns and let us know if you need any adjustments during the interview process, we’re here to support you. We also warmly encourage applications from people from underrepresented backgrounds.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/siteminder/senior-sales-executive-dach-berlin-184651","tags":["GTM - Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792194022},{"slug":"senior-research-manager-survey-data-innovation-hamburg-448825","company_name":"Statista","title":"(Senior) Research Manager – Survey Data & Innovation (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>Statista</strong>, we’re all about facts and data, for we are the world's leading business data platform. By providing reliable and easy-to-use data as well as various data analytics products and services, we empower people worldwide to make fact-based decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Hamburg in 2007, we have quickly grown into a global company with offices in major cities such as London, New York, Berlin and Tokyo. And we still have a lot of plans. Our constant growth does not only prove our success, but also keeps creating new development and career opportunities for our employees.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value and celebrate our diverse culture. You are welcome here for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or whether you prefer bar graphs to pie charts. Your story matters – keep writing it as part of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to join us?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve survey operations. Contribute to ongoing survey work and identify opportunities to improve our methods, tools, and processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore new approaches to consumer data. Lead projects assessing ways to collect or produce consumer data beyond online surveys, including behavioral data integration, data fusion, and synthetic data. Weigh their limitations against their potential value for client use cases. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and run pilots: Set clear objectives, test promising approaches, and make evidence-based recommendations about whether and how to use them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply AI to survey workflows. Identify where AI could improve data quality checks, survey production, or other processes. Test practical applications and help implement those that deliver measurable benefits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track the market. Follow how competitors and other research providers are developing their methods, data sources, and technologies. Turn relevant developments into proposals we can evaluate or test.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn findings into action. Present your conclusions clearly, invite challenge and discussion, and work with colleagues and stakeholders to put agreed improvements into practice.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong grounding in quantitative market research and hands-on experience with online surveys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving a research method, workflow, or data product, including assessing whether the change achieved its goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about emerging approaches, including AI, and the judgement to recognise both their potential and their limitations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to assess new approaches independently, think critically about their fit and impact, 