ct for customer quality, audits and escalations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead customer RMA and complaint handling, root cause analysis and 8D responses to agreed timelines.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure product compliance with RoHS, REACH, WEEE, conflict minerals reporting, UKCA and CE marking, and relevant safety and EMC standards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential experience and skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience in quality roles in semiconductors or electronics hardware, including creating and leading a quality function or team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience managing quality through outsourced manufacturing: foundries, OSATs, test houses and/or contract manufacturers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of ISO 9001 and hands-on experience building or running a certified QMS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of semiconductor qualification and reliability (JEDEC), failure analysis and</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awareness of data centre RAS assessments and HPC system qualification and certification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in core quality tools: 8D, FMEA, control plans, SPC, MSA and root cause analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling customer quality escalations with large, demanding customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in electrical or electronic engineering, materials science, physics or a related discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, confident communicator who can influence engineers, suppliers and executives, and hold partners to account.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willing to travel internationally, including to Asia and US, for supplier audits and customer quality reviews.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><