ght:1.5em">We're funded by leading investors at Index Ventures and Lightspeed Venture Partners, along with Factory, Conviction, A Star, General Catalyst, SV Angel, Databricks and others. We're fortunate to have the support of many amazing advisors, and 90+ angels across many industries, including the world's foremost experts in AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Product and Research Operations Manager to run the operational backbone of Cartesia's Voice function - supporting voice production for customers, talent sourcing and logistics, and voice delivery for Go-To-Market and Customer Success. You'll work directly alongside our Voice Production Lead and Voice Library Lead, and provide hands-on support across their respective work-streams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Part of your time will go toward cross-functional ad-hoc operations, including supporting growth initiatives.</p><h2><strong>Your Impact</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Voice Production &amp; Library - </strong>Support execution of voice production runs alongside the Voice Production Lead. Over time, you'll own day-to-day production and library health reporting, take on more locales and volume, and build automations to streamline the process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sourcing &amp; Talent logistics - </strong>Support voice sourcing alongside the Voice Library Lead. Build the systems to source, vet, and create voices for the voice library with voice acting talent as well as vendors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Voice Delivery &amp; Enablement -</strong> Own customer-facing voice engagements end to end, driving customers to be successful with our models. Drive voice-related GTM enablement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ad-hoc Strategy and Growth Projects -</strong> Support ad-hoc strategy &amp; operations work, including helping run events and marketing initiatives for Cartesia in London. Support Cartesia’s growth in international markets on a project by project basis.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3 - 6 years as an operator at a high-growth tech startup or in strategy consulting (MBB or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High agency - a proactive self-starter who can operate autonomously to get things done in ambiguous environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer-facing chops, with the ability to drive conversations with executives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Semi-technical - comfortable using tools like Cursor, Claude Code, etc to build lightweight systems, and understands core concepts of system design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine interest in operating with founder-level hunger, and real enthusiasm for voice and audio technology - you have opinions on it, not just interest</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes a strong candidate:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in the AI industry, especially in AI Strategy and Operations or Product Operations roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of going out of your way to get things done proactively</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Builds lightweight systems autonomously</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Detail-oriented under volume; maintains attention to detail even with large volume of tasks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credible in front of GTM teams and customers without needing a lead in the room</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>More Details</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏢 <strong>In-office policy: </strong>We’re an in-person team based out of offices in 🇺🇸 San Francisco, 🇬🇧 London and 🇮🇳 Bangalore. We love being in 