es.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Debug, maintain and improve our existing codebase.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Develop and execute unit tests and integration tests to ensure software reliability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Conduct performance profiling and stress testing to optimize system responsiveness.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Maintain clear, structured documentation for data models and ETL/ELT pipelines and codebases.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Collaborate closely with cross-functional teams, including client applications and cloud teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Stay adaptable, learning new technologies and contributing to various technical areas as needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Skills &amp; Experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Bachelor’s degree in computer science or a related field or equivalent proven experience in database and data pipeline development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Hands-on experience with code-driven data orchestration tools.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Solid experience with relational databases and SQL.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Strong Python language and OOP skills.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience in data modelling for both transactional systems and analytical systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Strong debugging, troubleshooting, and performance optimization skills.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Proficiency with Git, including active participation in code reviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Excellent communication and teamwork skills.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Keen in developing in-house tech stacks as well as utilizing off-the-shelf components to build a robust solution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Familiarity with CI/CD and database migration tooling.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Knowledge of REST/GraphQL or other API design methodologies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Familiarity with working in Linux based environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience with containers and container orchestration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience in Test-Driven Development (TDD), PyTest and software design patterns.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏝️ </strong>25 days annual leave + public holidays</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private healthcare with Vitality</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎄 Christmas shutdown days on top of leave allowance (2-4 per year usually)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚇 Office located within a 5-minute walk from Angel station</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏠 Hybrid working</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🪙 Biannual salary reviews</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥳 Summer &amp; Christmas staff parties</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍣 Free lunch bought in and after-work gathering/drinks every other Thursday in the office</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Employee referral scheme</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Make a real-world impact of revolutionising the construction industry</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you'd like to see the products and technology we have created so far on our journey you can view it in action through our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/@XYZReality/videos">YouTube</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.xyzreality.com/">Website</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/xyz-reality/senior-data-engineer-london-213866","tags":["Platform"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1792215630},{"slug":"design-operations-lead-london-263482","company_name":"Gen Digital","title":"Design Operations Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job Title:</strong> Design Operations Lead<br /><strong>Location:</strong> London, Hybrid (3 days in office)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Gen:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're not just a company; we're a global force. Fiercely committed to ensuring that everyone, everywhere, can live their lives digitally safe. Our family of brands, Norton, Avast, LifeLock, Avira, AVG, ReputationDefender and CCleaner, unite the brightest minds, the sharpest tech and the most diverse thinking to protect over 500 million people. And we've built an inclusive workplace, where your well-being is a priority because true success comes from a place of balance and authenticity. When you're thriving, you're unstoppable. So, bring us your bold ideas and passion that refuses to quit. The digital world isn't some distant reality, it's the world we live in, and we're ready for it. If you're ready to push boundaries and be part of something bigger, join #TeamGen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our hybrid work style (3 days in the London office) gives us the face-to-face time to have creative conversations, meaningful meetings, make quick decisions and build relationships. And it's flexible enough to give you the space to do your best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Design Operations Lead you will support the day-to-day operations of Gen's global product design organisation. You will work alongside product designers, researchers, design leaders, and cross-functional partners to improve the workflows, tools, and systems that help teams do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will bring structure to planning, delivery, handoffs, reviews, and team rituals. By making ways of working clearer and easier to scale, you will help the design organisation operate with greater visibility, consistency, and focus and help teams deliver better outcomes for our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be part of a global product design organisation working across Gen's family of digital safety brands. The team brings together product designers, researchers, design leaders, and cross-functional partners who collaborate to solve meaningful problems for people navigating the digital world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design Operations sits at the centre of this network, helping teams connect their plans, tools, rituals, and documentation so that creative work can move forward with less friction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive and facilitate core planning and collaboration cadences, including sprint planning, milestone reviews, retrospectives, and design critiques</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and implement workflow and process improvements, including automation, documentation, and tooling strategies that improve visibility and reduce friction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with design leads to create clear timelines, milestone plans, and delivery checkpoints that support accountability and informed decision-making</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and evolve project-tracking systems such as JIRA and Figma ensuring they remain useful, current, and aligned to team needs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain team documentation, briefs, review records, and other operational resources so that information is easy to find and act on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create structure around design handoffs, stakeholder reviews, and team rituals to empower designers and improve cross-functional collaboration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support continuous improvement through feedback loops, retrospective facilitation, and structured iteration on processes and ways of working</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a thoughtful organiser who understands that strong operations should enable great design, not get in its way. You are comfortable bringing clarity to complex work, coordinating across different perspectives, and improving processes in a fast-moving environment. You have a genuine appreciation for design and can build trust with creative, technical, and business partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Education: a degree or equivalent practical experience in design operations, UX, project or programme management, business, or a related field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5-7 years of experience in design operations, UX programme coordination, project management, or a related role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting a design, research, product, or similarly collaborative team in a complex organisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving workflows, planning cadences, documentation, or operational systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with modern design and delivery tools, including Figma, JIRA, ClaudeCode</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively across teams and levels of seniority</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent organisation and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and follow through on commitments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong planning, facilitation, and project coordination skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to analyse how work gets done, identify friction, and turn improvements into practical, repeatable ways of working</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence learning and managing tools, systems, and documentation practices that support design teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal Attributes:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious, pragmatic, and motivated by continuous improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative and relationship-oriented, with a calm and constructive approach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive and dependable, with strong ownership of details and follow-through</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adaptable and comfortable working in a fast-moving, global environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passionate about creating the conditions for designers and partners to do their best work</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Gen Digital, we are committed to supporting our employees' well-being and professional growth. Our comprehensive benefits package for UK team members includes:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellbeing: company-paid private medical insurance, dental and vision benefits, plus access to mental health and wellbeing support through our Employee Assistance Programme (EAP)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Financial Security: a Group Personal Pension Plan with auto-enrolment for eligible employees, together with the opportunity to purchase Gen stock through our Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited Paid Time Off: available once statutory annual leave has been used, plus company holidays and a range of leave options to support personal and family needs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tuition Reimbursement: up to £5,150 per calendar year for job-related accredited courses that support career development within Gen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wellness Reimbursement: up to $450 per year to cover fitness-related expenses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability Allowance: a $500 annual sustainable home improvement allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional Perks: access to adoption assistance, family support services, legal assistance plans and exclusive employee discounts</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What's Next:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your CV will be reviewed by the recruiter and hiring manager to understand the scope of your work, the impact you've delivered, and how your experience aligns with the role. If shortlisted, the recruiter will be in touch to set up a conversation to learn more about your background, what's motivating you, why you're interested in Gen and our products, and to go through the interview process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gen is an equal opportunity employer, and we're committed to fair, inclusive practices at every stage of the candidate and employee journey. Employment decisions are based on merit, experience and business needs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/gen-digital/design-operations-lead-london-263482","tags":["Global Customer Organization"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"GBR - London","created_at":1792215630},{"slug":"product-designer-london-105391","company_name":"Creativex","title":"Product Designer","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CreativeX&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CreativeX is B2B SaaS technology platform that helps global marketing teams make smarter creative decisions and elevate creative expression through the clarity of data. Our technology powers creative decision-making at some of the biggest brands in the world, including Google, Unilever, Pepsi, Bayer, Mondelez, Heineken, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use computer vision and other machine learning techniques to extract creative data from our client&#39;s digital advertising copy and transform those previously dark signals into a standardised data model at industrial scale. This creates a new, unique and powerful first party data set that represents the last and most impactful untapped reservoir of advertising performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s because multiple studies have shown that the &quot;Creative&quot; itself is responsible for half of sales lift online, higher than reach, targeting, brand, &amp;amp; recency combined. But creative impact has always been the least analysed and least understood component of a complex set of marketing variables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the problem CreativeX is focussed on solving. We&#39;re an end-to-end solution to ingest, process, and analyse content at scale. We help brands isolate creative elements so they can be analysed against downstream ad impact metrics, from clickthrough rates to brand lift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our objective is to help marketing organisations power every creative decision with data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Design Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Designer, you&#39;ll help shape the next generation of the CreativeX platform, taking problems from discovery through to shipped experiences across defined areas of the product. You&#39;ll be the design lead in a product trio alongside a Product Manager and an Engineering Lead, owning whether users want what we build and whether they can figure out how to use it, while sharing discovery, outcomes and trade-offs with your partners. CreativeX is a complex product with rich data, multiple user types and increasingly sophisticated AI capabilities, and as AI increases the volume and speed of creative production, you&#39;ll make that complexity work for marketers, helping them measure performance fast, find the patterns behind what&#39;s working and see whether their full set of ads is delivering the strategy. Our roadmap is framed as problems to solve, not screens to make, so we expect you to bring a point of view. Product Design is a small, hands-on team in a scale-up: you&#39;ll be trusted with real ownership early, and this hire is an important step in growing the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design for defined product areas, from understanding the problem through to working with Product and Engineering to ship the right experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get close to marketers and creative teams through customer conversations, research and usability testing, using what you learn to inform design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering in discovery to validate real problems, challenge assumptions and make sensible trade-offs between customer value, business needs and technical constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn creative data, insights and AI-powered capabilities into intuitive workflows, dashboards and decision-making tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for the platform, not just the feature, building on existing patterns and connecting experiences across CreativeX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use and extend our design system, creating and documenting patterns and components so they&#39;re implemented consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the quality bar through strong interaction and visual design craft, and by giving and receiving feedback in critiques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from what you ship, using customer feedback, product data and research to improve the experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In your first 90 days&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the CreativeX platform, our customers and our design system, and work as the design lead in your product trio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of a defined product area and ship, or get build-ready, your first piece of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our AI-powered product work and add to or improve patterns in our design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join customer conversations and use what you hear to shape your design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In your first year&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design for one or more product areas, taking work from discovery through to launch with little direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship work you can point to, using customer feedback and product data to show whether it solved the problem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build out new parts of our design system and make the product feel more coherent across areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how design works at CreativeX as the team grows, including supporting newer designers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of product design experience, with a portfolio that shows how you framed problems, explored options, made trade-offs and learned from what shipped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interaction and visual design craft, confident in Figma, prototyping and design systems, and familiar with Slack and Linear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using research, usability testing and customer feedback to inform design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems mindset and the ability to make complex information, workflows and data easy to understand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, collaborative communication: you challenge ideas constructively, take feedback well and know when to ship and learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with Product and Engineering in a product trio or small team, with real ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/em&gt; B2B SaaS, data-heavy or analytics products; marketing, advertising or martech; AI-powered products; mentoring junior designers; scale-up experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CreativeX, we encourage applicants of all backgrounds and identities to apply for roles that align with their own interests and career trajectory. If you fit the description above and see yourself in this role, we would love to see your application! &lt;em&gt;Unfortunately, we are unable to offer visa sponsorship at this time.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍎 Private Medical Insurance and Health Cash Plan&lt;br&gt;✈️ Generous time off + bank holidays&lt;br&gt;📚 Education budget to be used for individual learning experiences or grouped with your team for joint learning&lt;br&gt;🧘 Annual subscription to Calm and Headspace for your mental wellbeing&lt;br&gt;🎟 Monthly coaching to talk to a trained professional about career goals, relationships, and personal development&lt;br&gt;💵 Competitive salary including stock options, as we believe that everyone should have a stake in the business&lt;br&gt;🍼 4-month full pay parenting leave for all employees who have been with the company for one (1) year&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CreativeX provides equal employment opportunities for all applicants and employees.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As part of our commitment to maintaining a safe and secure workplace, CreativeX conducts standard right to work and background checks on all potential employees. This process is designed to verify the accuracy of information provided by candidates and to ensure a safe environment for all employees. Background checks are conducted via a secure third party application and in compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
