th senior leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard, and certify new OAs to the GTM builder motion, driving readiness from ramp through consistent execution and managing performance with clarity when expectations are not met.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Solutions Consultant managers and leaders on strategy for expansion and renewal across shared accounts, ensuring clear ownership for flat and at-risk renewals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Services leadership to identify complex implementation needs early, create clear handoffs, and ensure Services delivery accelerates workflow adoption and measurable value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the standard for product, AI, and workflow fluency across the team so OAs can help customers navigate new ways of working and build durable systems in Notion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent your team or region in leadership forums with clear signal on what's working, what needs investment, and where execution is breaking down</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Uphold excellence by coaching to the global OA methodology, quality rubric, and activity KPIs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Skills You’ll Need to Bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frontline management experience leading customer-facing GTM teams in B2B software, ideally across Customer Success, Solutions Consulting, Technical Account Management, Professional Services, Account Management, or post-sales strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience coaching teams through customer discovery, workflow design, adoption planning, value realization, renewals, expansion, or technical/workflow implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong coaching orientation: you can review a customer call, account plan, mutual success plan, or executive value narrative and identify specifically what needs to change — not just whether the outcome was good, but why and how to improve it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial instincts at the team level: able to read account health, renewal risk, adoption depth, expansion potential, and customer sentiment, then drive urgency without micromanaging every account.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep customer-facing discovery instincts, with the ability to understand business problems, map workflows, and translate goals into practical adoption and implementation plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience operating in a shared account ownership model with Sales, Solutions, Services, Support, or Implementation teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational rigor: you know how to build inspection cadences, coaching rituals, performance standards, and accountability systems that improve execution across a team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to develop talent from onboarding through consistent performance, including hiring to profile, setting clear expectations, coaching skill gaps, and managing performance with clarity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive communication skills: able to synthesize account patterns, customer risks, team performance, and cross-functional asks into clear signal for leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical fluency and presence as a trusted advisor. You do not need to build every workflow yourself, but you should be able to understand Notion systems, coach workflow design, and help your team troubleshoot adoption blockers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You operate with agency, urgency, and customer empathy, bringing structure to ambiguous problems and helping teams move from ideas to working systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to be an AI expert, but you’re curious, hands-on, and willing to adopt AI tools to work smarter, coach better, and help customers deliver better outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English and French</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Nice to Haves</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing in a consumption, usage-based, or product-led business where adoption signals matter as much as renewal or expansion outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record building high-performing frontline teams from an early stage: hiring to profile, structured onboarding, certification, coaching, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading teams through GTM motion changes, coverage-model shifts, or evolving commercial ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with flat, at-risk, or complex renewal accounts and helping teams return customers to a clear value path.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience partnering closely with Solutions Consulting, Sales, Services, or Implementation teams in a shared customer lifecycle model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with AI transformation, workflow automation, agents, or collaboration/work management software.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By clicking “Submit Application,” I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s Global Recruiting Privacy Policy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Onsite</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>A Note on AI</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need deep AI expertise for every role, but we do expect every Notino to be intellectually curious, drawn to tinkering and discovery, and excited to use AI as a real collaborator in their work. For some roles, AI fluency is a core requirement — when that’s the case, we'll say so explicitly in the qualifications. People who thr