amp; System Design:</strong> Own the end-to-end architecture for digital asset solutions, seamlessly integrating distributed ledger technology (DLT) with traditional market infrastructure (trading, clearing, settlement, custody, and CSD).</li><li><strong>Cross-Chain &amp; Network Topology:</strong> Design cross-chain topology combining permissioned chains for institutional and CCP operations (e.g., Hyperledger Besu, Canton Network) with public chains for DeFi distribution (Ethereum / L2).</li><li><strong>On-Chain Compliance &amp; Governance:</strong> Define regulatory compliance frameworks on-chain, utilizing regulated security-token standards (ERC-3643 / T-REX), KYC-whitelisted wallets, automated transfer restrictions, real-time AML screening (Chainalysis / Elliptic), and transaction reporting under MiFIR.</li><li><strong>Custody &amp; Key Management:</strong> Architect robust custody models around MPC solutions (e.g., Fireblocks, Taurus), incorporating hybrid frameworks to support bring-your-own-custody (BYOC) for institutional clients.</li><li><strong>Security &amp; Quality Standards:</strong> Establish code quality, code review, testing, and secure-by-design standards. Conduct threat modelling and lead security architecture prior to onboarding a dedicated security lead.</li><li><strong>AI-Augmented Software Delivery:</strong> Define, implement, and govern an AI-assisted software delivery process using coding assistants, smart-contract scaffolding, and AI-generated test suites while enforcing strict risk and review guardrails.</li><li><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partner with product, legal, regulatory, clearing, CSD, and client working groups to maintain alignment with business objectives and regulatory frameworks (e.g., DLT Pilot Regime, MiFID II, MiCA).</li><li><strong>Technical &amp; Operational Leadership:</strong> Make key build/buy/partner evaluations on blockchain networks, custody, and audit solutions. Guide team evolution as products move from build to operational phases, maintaining hands-on involvement during critical incidents.</li></ul><p></p><p>Requirements</p><ul><li><strong>Experience:</strong> Minimum 7 years of solution architecture experience, including at least 3 years dedicated to DLT or blockchain projects within high-value, 24/7 financial systems.</li><li><strong>DLT &amp; Distributed Systems Expertise:</strong> Deep fluency with EVM and permissioned chains (e.g., Canton, Hyperledger Besu).</li><li><strong>Regulated Token Standards:</strong> Hands-on experience with regulated security token standards (ERC-3643 / T-REX or equivalent), on-chain compliance models, and security considerations around smart contracts and cross-chain bridges.</li><li><strong>Capital Markets Knowledge:</strong> Strong working knowledge of capital markets settlement mechanisms (delivery-versus-payment, CSD operations, CCP/clearing) to effectively design system integrations.</li><li><strong>AI Engineering Competency:</strong> Proven ability to evaluate, select, and integrate AI tooling into the development lifecycle (e.g., testing, scaffolding) while establishing strict guardrails around prompt hygiene, secret security, and license provenance. Ability to specify in-product AI capabilities (e.g., anomaly detection) with proper risk controls.</li><li><strong>Leadership &amp; Communication:</strong> Strong decision-making skills and composure under pressure. Excellent stakeholder management skills to bridge technical, business, legal, and regulatory domains.</li><li><strong>Education:</strong> Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field. Professional certifications in cloud or blockchain technologies are advantageous.</li><li><strong>Work Arrangement:</strong> Openness to work onsite in Paris, France, 4 days per week.</li></ul><p>﻿</p><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Competitive annual salary (€100,000 – €120,000).</li><li>Key role within a high-visibility, zero-to-o