1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the technical follow-up of assigned components</strong> during the whole steps from concept to qualification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide hands-on technical support for component design and industrialisation</strong>, including trade-offs, interface definition, CAD and drawing reviews, design-for-manufacture and assembly, and resolution of technical issues during build and integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define and maintain the technical baseline</strong> for each component, including requirements, interfaces, standards, verification approach, acceptance criteria, configuration, and open technical points.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain a system-level view of component interfaces and constraints</strong>, including mechanical, fluidic, thermal, electrical, command, sensing, cleanliness, materials compatibility, safety, operations, and integration aspects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define and drive development, qualification, acceptance, and integration test strategies</strong>, including test objectives, setups, instrumentation, procedures, readiness reviews, execution, data analysis, and closure of findings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Review test results and supplier evidence</strong> to confirm performance, robustness, lifetime, environmental, interface, safety, production-repeatability, and other applicable requirements are met.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define and review relevant test campaigns</strong>, including functional performance, leakage, pressure and flow behaviour, response time, actuation, thermal and vibration environments, EMC, cleanliness, lifecycle performance, fault conditions, and production repeatability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead the technical interface with suppliers, manufacturing partners, special-process providers, and test houses</strong>, including review of deliverables, drawings, analyses, procedures, inspection evidence, deviations, non-conformances, and test packages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identify, communicate, and manage technical risks, anomalies, and corrective actions</strong>, including performance shortfalls, leakage, response issues, cleanliness and materials concerns, lifetime limitations, weak evidence, production variability, delivery risks, and integration constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support Huracan MAIT/AIT, integration, testing, and operations preparation</strong>, including readiness reviews, setup and instrumentation reviews, procedure reviews, test execution, troubleshooting, data assessment, recovery or retest decisions, and the capture of component limitations, monitoring needs, failure responses, and operational constraints.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Would Love To See From You</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering background in aerospace, mechanical, propulsion, fluids, electrical, instrumentation, or a related discipline, with experience in spacecraft, launch vehicles, industrial systems, or other safety-critical hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and developing hardware, including CAD, drawings, design reviews, manufacturing, assembly, integration, materials, tolerances, and applicable standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing the technical follow-up of suppliers and manufacturing partners through development, testing, qualification, delivery, integration, and anomaly resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical knowledge of component requirements, interfaces, verification, qualification, acceptance testing, failure modes, root-cause investigation, and component- or system-level test campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting AIT or equivalent integration and test activities, and the ability to assess the robustness of designs, manufacturing processes, test approaches, and supplier evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with applicable component standards, design practices, drawings, tolerances, materials, manufacturing processes, and aerospace or industrial standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work across disciplines, maintain ownership of technical topics, and communicate effectively with engineering, procurement, quality, MAIT/AIT, test, program, suppliers, manufacturing partners, and operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English; French and/or German are advantageous.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Skills And Behaviours<br /></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You keep the technical position clear even when ownership, supplier evidence, schedule, or integration constraints are messy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You judge component decisions by their spacecraft mission, safety, integration, cost, and schedule impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You make assumptions, evidence gaps, weak test results, open points, deviations, and emerging risks visible early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use testing and objective evidence to drive decisions, while remaining pragmatic about development speed and available resources.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You balance fast development with configuration, manufacturing, cleanliness, verification, qualification, and safety discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable going into the detail of a component, its interfaces, its test data, and its failure modes while keeping sight of the overall vehicle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build trust with suppliers, partners, engineers, and leadership through facts, clear decisions, and follow-through.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Exploration Company and why we think you will enjoy working here is:  </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Agile - we make decisions fast whilst keeping our goals and systems in mind </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Open and Collaborative - we are transparent about risks and obstacles, so that we can cooperate to overcome them  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a lot of Fun - we refuel our energy knowing we are democratising space. It’s a wonderful and rare opportunity, are YOU up for the challenge?  </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to hear from you if you wish to be a part of our journey. Please submit your CV now for immediate consideration and we will be in touch shortly. <br /> <br /><em>The Exploration Company is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status. Relocation assistance is provided for those willing to relocate including visa sponsorship where applicable.  </em><br /><br /><em><br />All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check, which will be subject to the country, role, and project you applied for. By submitting your application, you acknowledge and agree that any offer of employment may be conditional upon successful condition of this check. The Exploration Company partners with Zinc Work Limited located in the UK (Zinc), a third-party provider, to ensure this process as efficient and transparent as possible. <br /><br />If applicable, you will receive an email from Zinc upon acceptance of your offer with a link to a secure portal where you can provide the required information to Zinc. </em><br /></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/the-exploration-company/propulsion-engineer-huracan-components-bordeaux-14947","tags":["US & Future Programs"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Bordeaux, France","created_at":1792172418},{"slug":"hil-engineer-huracan-rocket-engine-bordeaux-105519","company_name":"The Exploration Company","title":"HIL Engineer — Huracan Rocket Engine","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Here at The Exploration Company, we are building spacecrafts for humanity.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>About the role<br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Exploration Company is developing Huracan, a cryogenic rocket engine. The engine integrates e-pumps, power electronics, valves, embedded software, and control systems. We are seeking a Hardware-in-the-Loop Engineer to develop and operate HIL platforms for verifying the ECU, PDU, Valve Controller, inverter, electric pumps, and associated software. You will connect real hardware to real-time simulations, automate testing and data analysis, and develop emulator hardware for sensors, actuators, interfaces, and subsystem behaviour. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will verify nominal and fault conditions while ensuring test repeatability, traceability, and early fault detection. You will work closely with propulsion, embedded-software, power-electronics, control-systems, and hardware engineers to validate Huracan from simulation through laboratory testing.<br /><br /></p><h2>Key responsibilities<br /></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build, and maintain the HIL test environment for our engine propulsion system, from engine controller board level up to the integrated propulsion subsystem </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and implement the hardware and software architecture of the propulsion HIL bench, including signal conditioning, load and fault-insertion hardware, and real-time targets </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate real-time plant models (e.g., feed system, valves, pumps and motors, combustion chamber, thermal behaviour) into NI VeriStand and close the loop with the engine control unit </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Emulate and simulate the sensors the controller depends on (e.g., pressure transducers, thermocouples and RTDs, flow meters, position and speed feedback) with flight-representative electrical characteristics </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Emulate or integrate actuators and power electronics, such as valve drivers, motor inverters, igniters, and their control units, as real hardware, electrical loads, or models </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop LabVIEW-based applications for desktop and real-time platforms (e.g., PXI, cRIO), including custom devices and bus interfaces (e.g., CAN, RS-422/485, Ethernet) </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement fault injection at the electrical and model level to verify engine start-up, shutdown, and abort sequences as well as FDIR behaviour </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support test execution, data acquisition, logging, and automated reporting during verification campaigns </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate and correlate simulation models against component-level and engine test data together with the propulsion team </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and maintain technical documentation, including architecture specifications, interface definitions, model and code documentation, and user guides </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug and troubleshoot across the bench, the models, and the unit under test, and continuously improve the test platform </p></li></ul><h2><strong>You will be in charge of</strong> </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivering a robust and scalable HIL platform whose models, I/O configuration, and test sequences can be reused across engine configurations and projects </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running control loops and plant models deterministically at the rates the engine controller requires, using NI hardware, LabVIEW RT, and FPGA where timing demands it </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Defining test automation workflows using NI TestStand and integrating them into the propulsion and system-level verification process </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinating closely with propulsion, avionics, and flight software engineers to ensure requirements traceability and test coverage </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping models, bench hardware, and test software under configuration control so that every test run is reproducible </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributing to the continuous evolution of our HiL infrastructure, with an emphasis on performance, reliability, and maintainability </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensuring all solutions meet space-grade quality and safety standards, aligned with project requirements </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-Have Skills and Qualifications</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Control Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building and operating HIL test benches for closed-loop control systems (e.g., engine, motor, or actuator controllers) </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in LabVIEW, including desktop and real-time application development </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with NI VeriStand in real-time test environments, including integration of simulation models (e.g., Simulink, FMU, or C/C++) </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience emulating sensors and actuators at the electrical level (e.g., analog, thermocouple/RTD, frequency and PWM, discrete I/O) and working with motor drives or inverters </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with NI TestStand for test automation and execution management </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of test platform architectures, hardware/software integration, and real-time systems </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong debugging and troubleshooting skills, with a structured and methodical approach </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to write and integrate Python scripts to extend test workflows or support automation tasks </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice-to-Have</strong> </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with LabVIEW FPGA, for example for high-speed sensor emulation or motor and inverter simulation </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in liquid rocket propulsion or in fluid and thermal system modelling </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with fault-insertion hardware and FDIR verification </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with ECSS standards or equivalent aerospace standards such as DO-178C </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting engine or integrated system test campaigns </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Exploration Company and why we think you will enjoy working here is:  </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Agile - we make decisions fast whilst keeping our goals and systems in mind </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Open and Collaborative - we are transparent about risks and obstacles, so that we can cooperate to overcome them  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a lot of Fun - we refuel our energy knowing we are democratising space. It’s a wonderful and rare opportunity, are YOU up for the challenge?  </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to hear from you if you wish to be a part of our journey. Please submit your CV now for immediate consideration and we will be in touch shortly. <br /> <br /><em>The Exploration Company is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status. Relocation assistance is provided for those willing to relocate including visa sponsorship where applicable.  </em><br /><br /><em><br />All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check, which will be subject to the country, role, and project you applied for. By submitting your application, you acknowledge and agree that any offer of employment may be conditional upon successful condition of this check. The Exploration Company partners with Zinc Work Limited located in the UK (Zinc), a third-party provider, to ensure this process as efficient and transparent as possible. <br /><br />If applicable, you will receive an email from Zinc upon acceptance of your offer with a link to a secure portal where you can provide the required information to Zinc. </em><br /></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/the-exploration-company/hil-engineer-huracan-rocket-engine-bordeaux-105519","tags":["US & Future Programs"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Bordeaux, France","created_at":1792172418},{"slug":"internal-event-manager-paris-484439","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Internal Event Manager - Paris","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re seeking an <strong>Internal Event Manager</strong> to lead our internal event strategy and execution. In this role, you’ll develop and implement a comprehensive events plan, manage our new event spaces, and collaborate with internal teams and external agencies to deliver exceptional experiences for Mistralers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and execute a strategy for internal events, ensuring alignment with Mistral’s culture and objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and manage events from start to finish, including logistics, vendor coordination, and on-site execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain relationships with vendors, venues, and service providers in Paris.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the primary contact for internal teams hosting events in our new HQ.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure events are delivered on time, within budget, and to the highest standards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we are looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least +6 years, with 3 years as an Event Manager or in a similar role, ideally in a corporate or tech environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational and project management skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and interpersonal abilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A network of trusted vendors and venues in Paris.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English and French.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">It would be ideal if you had:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of AV and technical event requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with CRM or event management software.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/internal-event-manager-paris-484439","tags":["Human Resources"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792172417},{"slug":"research-engineer-orchestral-paris-13953","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Research Engineer, Orchestral","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Research Engineer on the Orchestral team, you will help build the agentic platform we use to train and evaluate our models. Orchestral is the system our researchers rely on to run training and evaluation at scale — from the rollout engine that powers agentic workflows to the infrastructure that keeps their workloads running reliably. What you build becomes the foundation the whole science team works on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work will span the platform's core: the library, tooling, abstractions and rollout engine — including new capabilities like long-running tasks, subagents and RL features — and the machinery that runs data and jobs at scale, with a focus on resiliency, routing and request handling. You will own significant pieces end to end, from design to production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a software engineering role rather than an ML or infrastructure-operations one: RL or PyTorch experience is not required, and you will spend your time building the platform, not operating it. You will be building a distributed RL system, with the scientists as your users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and build the core of the Orchestral platform: the library, abstractions and tooling researchers use to train and evaluate models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and evolve the rollout engine, shipping new capabilities such as long-running tasks and subagents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run Orchestral as a production system: keep training and evaluation workloads reliable at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve how data and jobs flow through the platform as usage grows — scheduling, routing and request handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Treat researchers as your users: understand their workflows and turn recurring needs into robust, shared tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise the bar on engineering quality across the platform: testing, code review, CI/CD, observability and documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to open-source rollout-engine and agent-infrastructure projects where it benefits the platform.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience directly building and debugging complex distributed systems at scale, with an emphasis on reliability and scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python skills and solid software-design instincts: testing, code review, CI/CD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A builder mindset: you have constructed systems from the ground up, not just operated polished ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record in small teams running complex systems at scale — for example in finance, crypto or ad tech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-starter, low-ego and collaborative, with a product mindset toward your users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about ML and RL — this experience is not required, but a desire to learn is.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice-to-haves</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with Ray or similar distributed-computing frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open-source contributions, especially to rollout-engine or agent-infrastructure projects such as SLIME, verl or PrimeRL.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or working with agentic workflows and environments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowanc