yle="min-height:1.5em">• Excellent spoken and written English is mandatory; French/German is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Functional safety certification (e.g. TÜV FSEng) is a plus</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date: Immediately</strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/eh-group/ingenieur-securite-fonctionnelle-piles-a-combustible-nyon-3080","tags":["Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Nyon","created_at":1792215634},{"slug":"junior-product-designer-ui-ux-zurich-299042","company_name":"Ethon","title":"Junior Product Designer - UI/UX","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>You turn complex manufacturing data into interfaces factory teams rely on every day, working side by side with our engineers.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ethon was built to eliminate the trillion-dollar waste problem in manufacturing. We are the technology leader in Industrial AI, building agentic workflows that help manufacturers optimize cost, quality, and speed of production. We are a fast-growing team driving massive impact in one of the largest and most under-served industries in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We serve the world's top manufacturers across the globe. From Siemens and Bosch to Lindt and Roche, our customers trust us to make their factories run better. We are backed by leading investors like Index Ventures, General Catalyst, and Earlybird. Our team draws from Google, Meta, Palantir, MBB, and top manufacturing companies, all here for the same reason: giving manufacturers the technology to run every factory at unprecedented productivity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT IS THIS JOB ABOUT?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join our small design team and work directly with our engineers. At first you’ll focus on UI: building screens, components and flows for our platform, and helping our design system grow. Over time you’ll take on larger parts of the product end to end.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is what you’ll do:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn flows and concepts into detailed production-ready screens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and maintain components in Figma, keep them in sync with what’s in code, and notice when patterns start to drift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pair with developers, review builds, and make quick trade-offs when something doesn’t fit the sprint. Your designs ship; you don’t just hand off Figma files.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">When a shortcut hurts the experience, you say so, explain why, and propose an alternative. And you know when good enough is good enough.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join customer calls and factory visits, test ideas with our forward deployed engineers, and bring what you learn back into the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help where a startup needs it: website updates, sales decks and marketing visuals now and then.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT DO YOU NEED TO BRING?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">First and foremost, we believe in curious people who are eager to learn and grow. If you're passionate about cutting-edge tech and driving major impact in manufacturing, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to have done it all. We can teach you manufacturing, our product, and a lot about designing complex B2B software. We can’t teach you to care about the details, or to be curious about how things work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must-haves:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re fluent in English and comfortable with changing priorities. You know when to be scrappy and when to be thorough.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 1–3 years of professional experience designing digital products. Internships and working-student roles count if you shipped real work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong UI craft and have hands-on experience with a design system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re fluent in Figma (components, variants, auto layout, variables) and comfortable using AI tools for quick iterations and prototypes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy working closely with developers and understand enough about frontend to design things that can be built.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can explain and stand behind your design decisions, and you change your mind when someone has a better argument.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re curious about users, technology and how things get made, and you actively look for feedback so you can grow.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with B2B SaaS, dashboards or data-heavy products</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY IS ETHON RIGHT FOR YOU?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work from our office in the center of Zürich. You will be here three days a week, because the hardest problems get solved in person.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work alongside two senior designers, get regular design critiques, and sit close to the engineers who build what you design. Feedback loops are short, access to founders is direct.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additionally, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performance-based career &amp; growth paths</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">On-site work with significant scope for flexible schedules</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation including stock options giving you a stake in Ethon's long-term success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vacation bonus if you take two consecutive weeks of vacation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning budget for courses, conferences, and coaching</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like your kind of work, we would like to meet you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're committed to building a team that reflects the diverse world we live in. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, and we especially welcome voices traditionally underrepresented in tech.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HOW TO APPLY</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Send us your CV and a portfolio with 2–3 case studies, at least one showing detailed UI work. Tell us briefly what you did yourself and what the team did.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our interview process includes a short design challenge during the on-site, so you can show us how you work.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/ethon/junior-product-designer-ui-ux-zurich-299042","tags":["Product & Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1792204837},{"slug":"customer-architect-150019","company_name":"Elastic","title":"Customer Architect","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale — unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data — securing and protecting private information more effectively — Elastic’s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are actively seeking a Customer Architect with an understanding of technology and hands-on experience in key IT domains, notably Observability, Cybersecurity, and Enterprise Search. You should possess a strong technical background, preferably with experience in cloud-based software solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value individuals who are passionate about staying at the forefront of technology trends with a growth mindset and excited to learn and implement new technologies. While previous experience with Elastic solutions is not a prerequisite, an eagerness to adopt our suite of solutions and apply them effectively to solve our customers&#39; challenges is critical. This key role involves not only driving the consumption of our Elastic solutions by aligning them with customer business objectives but also onboarding customers, securing adoption, and facilitating expansion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Customer Architect, you will be the Trusted Technical Advisor, working in tandem with the customer and complementary groups like Field and Services Teams to ensure that Elastic solutions are exceeding customer’s expectations. . Your technical expertise, eye for business, and ability to deliver value will accelerate and improve the customer experience leading to customer continued satisfaction and expansion within the elastic portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your role, a crucial part of your responsibility is defining and communicating the technical success criteria for our customers. This involves crafting detailed Technical Success Plans tailored to the specific customers goals and critical metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technical Success Plans act as a roadmap, outlining the optimal consumption and deployment of Elastic solutions in the customer&#39;s environment. They detail the necessary steps for implementation, highlight achievements for successful consumption or expansion, and provide and effectiveness aligned to the customer’s business goals. By actioning this plan , you will be seen as the trusted advisor, guiding the customer towards achieving their desired outcomes, thereby ensuring their success and satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From providing technical guidance and sharing standard methodologies to aligning technical objectives with the customers&#39; business goals, your work is instrumental in facilitating smooth adoption, sustained usage, and increased consumption of our solutions. This hands-on role requires you to be proactive, with a keen understanding of our customers&#39; technical landscape and a commitment to making their journey with Elastic solutions successful and valuable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your chief aim will be to ensure the customer derives significant value, eliminate technical frictions, and propel the uptake and application of Elastic solutions, with the ultimate goal of growing annual recurring revenue (ARR).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate closely with the account team, including the Account Executive and the Solutions Architect (Pre-sales engineer), to provide ongoing technical coverage and support, while the account team focuses on identifying new deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define the technical success plan for each customer, outlining the optimal use of Elastic solutions to achieve their business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure a successful technical customer journey, from onboarding to adoption, while continuously driving the consumption of Elastic solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand and articulate the value proposition of Elastic solutions and align them with the customer&#39;s business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work closely with customers to identify and eliminate technical frictions, promoting a smoother adoption and implementation of Elastic solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liaise between customers and support, as necessary, to ensure an optimized support resolution experience smoothing the adoption curve for the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a hands-on technical authority, collaborate with the Service Team to deliver personalized, frictionless solutions that meet the unique needs of each customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop a comprehensive understanding of the customer&#39;s business needs and translate these into technical requirements for Elastic solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find opportunities for expansion, at which point the account team takes over to expand the subscription, aiming to grow annual recurring revenue (ARR).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Foster ongoing customer relationships, ensuring that customers continue to increase their utilization of Elastic solutions, further driving ARR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Continuously review and assess customer consumption of Elastic solutions, proactively suggesting upgrades and enhancements that increase value and drive further consumption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The nature of the work that you will be doing will require a high percentage of work onsite with customers, and you should be expected to travel as a result of this requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Systems, or a related field highly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German &amp;amp; English is required for this role. Fluency in French is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Validated experience in a similar role such as Solutions Architect, Technical Consultant, or Pre-sales Engineer, with hands-on experience with Elastic solutions or equivalent technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experienced with one or more Elastic solutions (Observability, Security, Enterprise Search) or the Elastic stack (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana) and how to align them with business objectives is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong social skills, with the ability to establish relationships with customers and team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving skills, with a track record of delivering innovative solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to lead multiple projects simultaneously and meet deadlines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-PF1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Information - We Take Care of Our People&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a distributed company, diversity drives our identity. Whether you’re looking to launch a new career or grow an existing one, Elastic is the type of company where you can balance great work with great life. Your age is only a number. It doesn’t matter if you’re just out of college or your children are; we need you for what you can do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to have parity of benefits across regions and while regulations differ from place to place, we believe taking care of our people is the right thing to do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pay based on the work you do here and not your previous salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage for you and your family in many locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to craft your calendar with flexible locations and schedules for many roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous number of vacation days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase your impact - We match up to $2000 (or local currency equivalent) for financial donations and service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 40 hours each year to use toward volunteer projects you love&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embracing parenthood with minimum of 16 weeks of parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Different people approach problems differently. We need that. Elastic is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating an inclusive culture that celebrates different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, disability status, or any other basis protected by federal, state or local law, ordinance or regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome individuals with disabilities and strive to create an accessible and inclusive experience for all individuals. To request an accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please email &lt;a ----- ----- class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;We will reply to your request within 24 business hours of submission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws, view posters linked below:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WHD/legacy/files/fmlaen.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA)&lt;/a&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Poster;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/ofccp/pdf/pay-transp_%20English_formattedESQA508c.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision&lt;/a&gt; Poster; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WHD/legacy/files/eppabw.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA)&lt;/a&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Poster and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/OFCCP/regs/compliance/posters/pdf/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Know Your Rights&lt;/a&gt; (Poster)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Elasticsearch develops and distributes technology and information that is subject to U.S. and other countries’ export controls and licensing requirements for individuals who are located in or are nationals of the following sanctioned countries and regions: Belarus, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, or Russia, including the Ukrainian territories annexed by Russia (The Crimea region of Ukraine, The Donetsk People&#39;s Republic (DNR), The Luhansk People&#39;s Republic (LNR), Kherson or Zaporizhzhia). If you are located in or are a national of one of the listed countries or regions, an export license may be required as a condition of your employment in this role. Please note that national origin and/or nationality do not affect eligibility for employment with Elastic.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.elastic.co/legal/applicant-privacy-statement&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.elastic.co/legal/applicant-privacy-statement&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1611068262479000&amp;amp;usg=AFQjCNG3orAPk5sJIr9WVm0ZDxYw82c5DA&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for our Privacy Statement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/elastic/customer-architect-150019","tags":["Customer Architects - EMEA"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792194928},{"slug":"sales-engineer-technical-sales-manager-root-419109","company_name":"Phenogyag","title":"Sales Engineer / Technical Sales Manager","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;PHENOGY AG is a leading innovator of battery energy storage technologies and solutions for the green electrification of the planet. Our team members work on future-proof and sustainable battery systems that are powerful, safe, and robust – with circularity as a central principle. Our technology partner network spans leading battery research institutes. PHENOGY is an environmentally and socially conscious enterprise. We are committed to fostering prosperity for the people and our planet, ensuring sustainable growth – starting in the area of our greatest expertise and impact: energy storage solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We energize the future.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;PHENOGY is seeking curious, entrepreneurial-minded energy pioneers to help shape our vision, systems, and growth; playing a key-role as we launch into our ambitious future. If you’re inspired by our mission, values, and drive to change how we energize the future — we’d love your application.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Your Role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You connect customer requirements, PHENOGY’s technology and profitable commercial execution. You turn customer needs into technically feasible, commercially attractive BESS solutions and independently drive opportunities to contract closure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Tasks &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customers &amp;amp; develop solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Analyse business models, load profiles, site and grid connection conditions, and investment criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Identify technical limitations and execution risks early and keep customer expectations realistic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customization &amp;amp; lighthouse projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Define scope, effort and cost of customization and how it is recovered: direct payment, volume-based recovery or approved strategic investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Identify lighthouse references and turn them into repeatable offerings and follow-on business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win profitable business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Own opportunities from qualification through proposal and negotiation to contract closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Drive customer relationship in all forms (workshops, project opportunities, tenders, …)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Build business cases (TCO, payback, ROI) and optimize configuration, scope and pricing; apply disciplined bid/no-bid decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feasibility &amp;amp; handover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Validate delivery feasibility with Engineering, Operations, Service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Hand over complete specifications, exclusions, risks and acceptance criteria to the delivery team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voice of the customer &amp;amp; sales discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Feed structured customer, competitor and win/loss insights into Product Management and Engineering; support new product introductions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;– Keep CRM and rolling forecast accurate; protect margin through scope control and sound payment milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must-haves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in electrical, energy or industrial engineering or a comparable field – equivalent practical experience is equally relevant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in technical sales, sales engineering, application engineering or solution sales for BESS, renewables, power electronics or industrial energy solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound understanding of BESS (batteries, inverters, system integration, controls, EMS) and applications such as peak shaving, self-consumption, renewable integration, backup power and market participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building customer business cases and communicating the financial value of technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tenders, technical specifications, proposals and negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage several opportunities and customer projects in parallel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent German and English&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German and further languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning first customer projects into repeatable solutions or broader market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software and service business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management experience in renewable energy or storage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Join a high-caliber environment that enables you to develop your full potential, shape your job, and take ownership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Participate in the development of PHENOGY and inspire the world to transition to sustainable energy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Become part of our eco-passionate expert team - a first-class team all around.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Benefit from flexible work hours as well as remote and on-site working in a modern sustainable office&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Enjoy various events, an amazing coffee machine, and the occasional coffee from our CEO (acting Barista)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;At PHENOGY, we highly value diversity, equality, and inclusion. It makes our company stronger. &lt;strong&gt;Our philosophy: one mindset, many minds.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;For recruitment and staffing agencies: PHENOGY works exclusively with selected recruitment partners under formal agreements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We do not accept unsolicited candidate submissions from agencies and assume no liability for claims made by unauthorized recruiters regarding our recruitment processes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/phenogyag/sales-engineer-technical-sales-manager-root-419109","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Root","created_at":1792194925},{"slug":"machine-learning-engineer-applied-ai-zurich-427794","company_name":"Bjak","title":"Machine Learning Engineer, Applied AI","description":"<h2><strong>About</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are over 5 billion users using basic applications today such email, notes, tasks, calendar and they're not AI-native. Our mission is to build proactive applications for anyone in the world, who are not used to complex prompting. We aim to bring intelligence to conversations, errands, organising and workflows, with minimal to no prompting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first application is an agent-first mobile communication app. We believe building applications that users use daily for communication, coordination and collaboration needs will help integrate AI into their lives. The net effect is to eliminate misinformation, achieve low coordination costs, enable high quality tasks and collaboration at scale with minimal or little prompting.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve ML systems that power our AI-native applications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on classification, retrieval, ranking, personalization and evaluation, taking ownership from model development to production deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is for engineers who enjoy solving practical ML problems, improving model quality and shipping reliable systems used by real users.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Focus</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve ML models for classification, ranking, retrieval and personalization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop efficient classifiers and optimize model accuracy, precision, latency and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve search relevance and context retrieval using embeddings, hybrid search and reranking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build personalization models that learn from user behavior while respecting privacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop evaluation pipelines, labeled datasets and metrics to measure model quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fine-tune and adapt existing models when supported by sufficient data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain ML training, inference and deployment pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug production issues, monitor model performance and ship improvements based on real-world feedback.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Tech Stack</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PyTorch / JAX</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embeddings, vector search and ranking models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production ML systems and inference pipelines</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Ideal Experience</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong foundations in machine learning and modern neural architectures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building and deploying ML models in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in classification, ranking, retrieval, recommendation systems or personalization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of model evaluation, experimentation and performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable writing production-quality code and working with real-world datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to balance model quality, latency, cost and reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership, problem-solving skills</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Outcomes</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ML models in production meet expected accuracy, relevance, latency and reliability targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Classification and ranking improvements deliver measurable gains in model quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluation pipelines identify regressions and support reliable model releases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Training, inference and data pipelines are robust, reproducible and maintainable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model improvements are driven by real-world feedback and measurable results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates effectively with engineering and product teams to deliver reliable ML-powered features.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>How We Work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best products in the world are built by small, world-class teams. We are a high-talent-density, hands-on team. We make decisions collectively and move quickly, balancing high-quality work with continuous learning.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining our team requires the ability to bring structure, exercise judgment and execute independently. Our goal is to put a truly magical product into the hands of our users.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Interview Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If there appears to be a fit, we'll reach out to schedule 3, but no more than 4 interviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applications are evaluated by our technical team members. Interviews will be conducted virtually and/or onsite.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value transparency and efficiency, so expect a prompt decision. If you've demonstrated the exceptional skills and mindset we're looking for, we'll extend an offer to join us.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/bjak/machine-learning-engineer-applied-ai-zurich-427794","tags":["ActAI Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1792194022},{"slug":"research-engineer-zurich-327456","company_name":"Sereact GmbH","title":"Research Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<h1>Research Engineer, Manipulation Data &amp; Teleoperation — Zurich</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role owns the data generation layer of Sereact's VLA stack: teleoperation systems and data collection infrastructure that feed Cortex, built from our Zurich research hub.</p><h2>About Sereact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sereact is a Series B embodied-AI company. Cortex, our VLA model, is deployed in live warehouse robotic cells across the EU and US. Zurich is our newest research hub, focused on the manipulation and control problems that sit underneath Cortex.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a Research Engineer position. It is scoped to the data generation layer of the VLA stack: teleoperation hardware and software, retargeting pipelines that map human demonstrations onto robot hands, and the data collection infrastructure that feeds Cortex. It requires building the systems that produce the data those models train on, and working closely with the training team on what that data needs to look like.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and operate teleoperation systems for dexterous manipulation, including retargeting algorithms that map human hand and arm motion onto robot end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and maintain scalable, UMI-style data collection hardware and software that other engineers at Sereact rely on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmark control and retargeting approaches using rigorous, human-factors-informed methodology</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instrument and support the physical robots deployed in the Zurich hub, including day-to-day work on the control stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the model-training team to define what data they need and close the loop on data quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tooling or infrastructure outside your immediate brief when it unblocks the wider team</p></li></ul><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc (or equivalent, in progress) in robotics, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field, with a thesis or capstone project on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building a data collection device or system for robot learning (UMI or a comparable system), not just operating one someone else built</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of retargeting algorithms for mapping human input onto robot hands or end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1 to 2 years of combined research, internship, or industry experience in robotics, mechatronics, or a related engineering discipline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software and systems engineering skills strong enough to build and maintain infrastructure other engineers rely on, not only research-grade prototypes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working as an individual contributor in a small, still-forming team</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A conference submission on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting where the candidate is an author (an MSc thesis submitted to a venue like CoRL counts; supervising a student team whose own work was later published does not)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teaching or TA experience in a robotics course</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some exposure to large-model training, even without an independent training record</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A concrete example of building something outside the formal role brief because the team needed it</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zurich Area, Switzerland: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our Zurich office, offering a vibrant ecosystem for robotics and AI.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free meals at the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours and the option to work from home when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct collaboration with founders and world-leading AI experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to large-scale compute clusters and proprietary robotic datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A key role in shaping the future of embodied AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation and a relocation package for the Zurich area</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/sereact-gmbh/research-engineer-zurich-327456","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792183219},{"slug":"solutions-architect-zurich-303054","company_name":"databricks","title":"Solutions Architect","description":"&lt;p&gt;FEQ128R7&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Solutions Architect, you will lead the technical strategy for your customers — owning architecture discussions, driving platform adoption, and serving as a trusted advisor to customer technical leads and architects. You combine deep technical expertise with strategic thinking to position Databricks as the foundation of your customers’ data and AI strategy. You are developing a technical specialization (archetype) and are recognized within your team for depth in a specific domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end technical strategy for your accounts, from initial discovery through production deployment and consumption growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex architecture discussions — designing scalable, production-grade solutions spanning data engineering, ML/AI, and real-time analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted technical advisor to customer architects, engineering leads, and Directors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical wins in competitive scenarios by demonstrating Databricks’ differentiation through custom-built solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and declare an emerging technical specialization (archetype) — becoming a go-to resource for your team in that domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate cross-functional resources (DSAs, SSAs, Partners) to deliver comprehensive solutions for complex customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence product direction by providing structured feedback on customer requirements and competitive gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in solutions architecture, data engineering, technical pre-sales, or a senior hands-on technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding proficiency in Python and SQL — you must demonstrate live coding, debugging, and solution-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in distributed data systems architecture: designing scalable pipelines, streaming architectures, lakehouse patterns, and cloud-native data platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient on the Databricks Platform (or demonstrated ability to achieve proficiency rapidly) with a developing technical specialization in one area (e.g., real-time/streaming, ML/AI, data governance, migrations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead architecture discussions with senior technical stakeholders — whiteboarding, design reviews, and trade-off analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with production deployments on public cloud (AWS, Azure, or GCP), including infrastructure, security, and governance considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of driving platform adoption and consumption growth within accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills — able to translate complex architectures into business value for both technical and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a quantitative discipline (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks certifications (Data Engineer, ML, Platform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with competitive platforms (Snowflake, AWS native services, Azure Synapse) — understanding the landscape you&#39;ll position against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a data/AI company or cloud provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry domain expertise (Financial Services, Healthcare, Retail, Media, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/databricks/solutions-architect-zurich-303054","tags":["Field Engineering - Other"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1792173335},{"slug":"machine-learning-certification-researcher-zurich-203268","company_name":"Destinusgroup","title":"Machine Learning Certification Researcher","description":"<p><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p>Imagine pioneering the mathematical and logical foundations that enable AI to fly safely in real-world, safety-critical aviation. As a Machine Learning Certification Researcher, you will address one of the most fundamental challenges in modern AI: proving that ML models are safe, reliable, and mathematically sound for deployment in autonomous flight. Your work will bridge the gap between cutting-edge statistical learning theory and formal aviation certification frameworks, building upon previous work (EASA CoDANN I and II, and FAA report DOT/FAA/TC-21/48), and putting real-world systems to the test.</p><p>At Destinus, we are shaping the future of defense through high-speed, autonomous flight technologies. We develop next-generation unmanned aerial systems that deliver greater speed, precision, and efficiency, supporting governments and defense organizations in mission-critical operations worldwide. Daedalean AG, the AI and autonomy hub of the Destinus Group, plays a key role in this vision—developing safety-critical AI systems at the intersection of advanced research and real-world aviation. Enabling machines to perceive, understand, and make decisions in real time, we combine aerospace engineering and artificial intelligence to build the next generation of autonomous flight systems, driving innovation where it matters most.</p><p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><p>• AI Certification Strategy: Analyze our existing AI certification strategy and help adapt it—or pioneer entirely new strategies—to certify different supervised ML.</p><p>• EASA Framework Alignment: Connect mathematical guarantees, technical arguments, and model evaluations to the EASA W-shaped process for AI certification in aviation, ensuring our research aligns with the latest regulatory guidelines.</p><p>• Theoretical Foundation &amp; Modeling: Conduct research into statistical learning theory, generalization bounds, and mathematical guarantees for deep neural networks operating under dynamic real-world conditions.</p><p>• Uncertainty Quantification: Apply statistics and stochastic processes to model environmental uncertainties and sensor noise, and to quantify confidence in performance metrics.</p><p>• Literature &amp; Proof Evaluation: Critically evaluate academic literature, mathematical proofs, and engineering assumptions with peer-review rigor to identify safety limitations and theoretical gaps in state-of-the-art AI.</p><p>• Regulatory &amp; Audit Justification: Construct robust, logical arguments and technical justifications that translate complex, high-dimensional empirical data into structured evidence for safety audits and certification frameworks.</p><p>• Algorithmic Validation: Write clean, reproducible code in Python to test theoretical hypotheses, validate certification mechanisms, and benchmark model safety frameworks.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What You'll Need</strong></p><p><strong>Machine Learning Theory &amp; Mathematics</strong></p><p>• ML Theory &amp; Statistical Learning: Deep understanding of statistical learning theory, generalization bounds, and the mathematical foundations of deep neural networks.</p><p>• Statistics &amp; Stochastic Processes: Strong background in advanced probability, statistical modeling, and stochastic processes.</p><p>• Python Engineering: Proficiency in Python with the ability to write clean, reproducible code (can also be learned on the job provided strong theoretical foundations and basic Python coding).</p><p><strong>Research Rigor</strong></p><p>• Scientific Research Methodology: Demonstrated capability or background in conducting comprehensive literature reviews, identifying gaps in current state-ofthe-art AI, and synthesizing complex academic concepts into actionable engineering frameworks (can also be learned on the job if you possess a strong quantitative baseline).</p><p>• Peer Review Expertise: Ability or experience in the peer-review process—capable of critically evaluating mathematical proofs, algorithmic assumptions, and research papers to assess their validity and limitations.</p><p><strong>Education</strong></p><p>• Currently pursuing or recently completed a Master’s, or PhD in Computer Science, Mathematics, Theoretical Statistics, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related quantitative research field.</p><p></p><p><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p>• Critical Thinking &amp; Healthy Skepticism: You possess a strong spirit of questioning everything. You naturally challenge conventional ML assumptions, probe for hidden edge cases, and refuse to take empirical accuracy at face value without rigorous proof.</p><p>• Logical Argument Building: You have an exceptional ability to construct robust, airtight logical arguments and technical justifications. You can translate complex empirical observations into structured, defensible evidence that satisfies strict </p><p>engineering and regulatory scrutiny.</p><p>• Thrives in Ambiguity: You are motivated by hard, unsolved mathematical problems at the intersection of theoretical computer science, safety engineering, and real-world flight operations</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/machine-learning-certification-researcher-zurich-203268","tags":["Defense & Space","R&D & Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1792171223},{"slug":"senior-manager-medical-excellence-international-zug-255570","company_name":"Bridgebio","title":"Senior Manager, Medical Excellence, International","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Director, Medical Excellence &amp;amp; Operations, International, and work closely with International Medical Affairs, Field Medical, Clinical Development, Commercial, Legal and Regulatory colleagues to strengthen medical excellence across BridgeBio. Your primary purpose will be to lead medical excellence initiatives across the Medical Affairs organization, such as scientific communications, field medical, training and other medical excellence priorities as the business evolves. This role requires effective collaboration with Medical Directors, cross-functional colleagues and external experts to ensure scientifically rigorous, consistent and compliant communications and practices. The ideal candidate combines deep expertise in scientific/medical communications with strong project management experience and stakeholder management skills, and thrives on delivering priorities in a fast-paced, hands-on environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of scientific communication plans from an international perspective (i.e., core scientific narratives, key messages and Q&amp;amp;A documents), in close collaboration with Medical Directors and cross-functional brand teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop high-quality scientific and medical education content for congresses, symposia, advisory boards, internal training and other settings, ensuring alignment with the medical strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Regulatory and Medical reviewers to ensure all scientific and medical communications are accurate, balanced and compliant, in line with the Medical, Legal and Regulatory (MLR) review process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design and delivery of onboarding, training and continuous learning programs for Medical Affairs, including building scientific and therapeutic area capability across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with medical communications agencies, medical writers and other vendors to ensure high-quality, on-time, on-budget deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the review, evaluation and compliant administration of independent medical education grants, scientific sponsorships and related third-party contracting, partnering with Legal, Compliance and Finance to ensure appropriate governance and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of standards, processes, tools and best practices that elevate medical excellence across areas such as Field Medical, insights generation &amp;amp; analysis, key performance indicators, training and other Medical Affairs priorities as business needs evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is an office role and requires in-office collaboration 2-3 days per week in our Zug office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No relocation is offered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel (approximately 10-20%) may be required to support scientific congresses, advisory boards, training sessions and internal meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in life sciences, pharmacy, medicine, or a related scientific discipline is required; an advanced degree (PhD, PharmD, MD, or MSc) is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of Medical Affairs experience in the biotech/pharmaceutical industry, in one or more of the following areas: scientific/medical communications, field medical, medical training, or related medical excellence functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scientific writing and editing skills, with the ability to translate complex clinical and scientific data into clear, accurate, audience-appropriate materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience developing scientific platforms, key messages, and training or capability-building programs in partnership with cross-functional medical and clinical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing external vendors/agencies and navigating MLR review processes; familiarity with grants, sponsorships, or contracting processes is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Versatile and adaptable, able to shift between medical excellence priorities as business needs evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management and stakeholder management skills; experience in rare disease is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English; additional language skills are an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market-leading compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model — we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
