uality in a production setting, with real familiarity with control plans, inspection methods, measurement systems, and process capability.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supplier quality experience, including auditing suppliers and holding them to standard.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured problem solving and root cause analysis, with a track record of permanently closing out recurring defects.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of product certification processes and the evidence they require, ideally in energy, power equipment, or another regulated product category. Exposure to both European and US regimes is a strong advantage.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The judgment to know which controls are essential at low volume and which can wait, and the confidence to hold a quality position under schedule pressure.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working across time zones and influencing a site you are not physically based at, including building quality capability remotely.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Especially compelling</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fuel cell, battery cell, or similar electrochemical assembly experience.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with cleanliness-critical or contamination-sensitive assembly processes.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting a technology transfer between sites or countries, and establishing quality at the receiving end.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience qualifying and auditing contract manufacturers or system integrators.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li>