D reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a hands-on scientist-engineer to help build our next-generation DNA synthesis platform, enabling high-throughput, cost-effective production of large and diverse DNA libraries. You'll work at the intersection of chemistry, materials science, bioengineering, and hardware development, designing and building prototypes, running experiments, and optimizing processes to turn new synthesis technologies into reliable, scalable production systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">DNA synthesis is a fundamental part of our protein engineering platform. We're developing new approaches to dramatically increase synthesis throughput while reducing cost and turnaround time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with our scientific and engineering teams to develop and prototype new DNA synthesis technologies. Your focus will be on translating scientific concepts into working hardware and experimental systems, designing and building prototypes, testing different approaches, and continuously improving their performance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a highly hands-on, interdisciplinary role combining experimental science with practical engineering. You'll take ownership of prototype development, experimental validation, and process optimization, helping move promising technologies from early concepts to reliable, scalable systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who enjoys building things, solving technical problems, and working across disciplines. You don't need to be an expert in DNA synthesis, but you should have strong scientific fundamentals, an engineering mindset, and experience turning ideas into working prototypes.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build, and test prototypes for next-generation DNA synthesis technologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate scientific and technical requirements into practical engineering designs and experimental setups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope and evaluate different technical approaches, components, materials, and equipment for prototype development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and optimize the chemistry, materials, and processes underlying the synthesis platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and execute experiments to characterize performance, identify limitations, and improve reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with mechanical, electronics, software, and automation engineers to develop integrated experimental systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot complex technical problems across chemistry, hardware, and process engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop analytical methods and quality control strategies to measure performance and guide optimization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help scale successful prototypes into robust, reproducible systems suitable for routine production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with external suppliers and engineering partners to source components, evaluate technologies, and accelerate development.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong background in chemical engineering, chemistry, materials science, bioengineering, mechanical engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience designing, building, and testing experimental setups, prototypes, or laboratory equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of chemistry, materials, or process engineering, with the ability to apply these fundamentals to practical engineering challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing and optimizing experimental processes, including systematic troubleshooting and performance characterization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across hardware and experimental science, translating scientific requirements into practical engineering solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selecting components, evaluating technical trade-offs, and iterating on prototype designs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experimental skills, including designing experiments, analyzing data, and making decisions based on results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independent, resourceful, and comfortable working on open-ended technical problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A practical, hands-on approach to engineering, with a focus on building, testing, and improving systems rather than purely theoretical development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with DNA or oligonucleotide synthesis, including chemical or enzymatic approaches, is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with solid-phase synthesis, surface chemistry, or chemical process development is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with microfluidics, high-throughput dispensing, or array-based technologies is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with laboratory automation, instrumentation, or custom hardware development is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CAD, electronics, fluidics, or mechanical prototyping is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience scaling experimental technologies from proof of concept to production is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Programming and data analysis experience, particularly in Python, is a plus.</p></li></ul><h2>Details</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Lausanne, Switzerland (on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Type:</strong> Full time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We review applications on a rolling basis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/dna-synthesis-platform-engineer-lausanne-166381","tags":["Biology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792064438},{"slug":"production-scientist-senior-lausanne-16629","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Production Scientist (Senior)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a lab technician position. This is a senior scientist who owns assay quality, data QC and controls, and production troubleshooting across the entire experimental pipeline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The production team runs 150+ experiments per month across expression, BLI, SPR, thermostability, and enzyme activity. When something goes wrong (failed expression, anomalous binding data, instrument artifacts), this person diagnoses the root cause and fixes it. As the assay and instrumentation portfolio expands, this person translates new R&amp;D methods into production-ready protocols, builds robust methods that junior technicians can execute reliably, and designs comprehensive controls that enable automated QC and data processing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a player-coach position. You will still run experiments personally, especially as you integrate into the lab, but you will also elevate the whole team's capabilities.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot production failures across the full pipeline. A batch of proteins isn't expressing: is it the construct design, the expression system, or the media? BLI sensorgrams look noisy: is it the sensor tips, the sample prep, or an instrument issue? You figure it out, fix it, and make the cause easier to identify next time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and document SOPs for new assays as the portfolio expands. Take methods from the R&amp;D team and make them production-ready: robust, reproducible, and executable by junior technicians without hand-holding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor a growing production team. Set quality standards, review data, train new hires, and build a culture where people flag problems early instead of hiding them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work at the intersection of biology, automation, and QC. Collaborate with researchers, laboratory technicians, and automation engineers on protocol optimization for work cells, and with software on LabOS protocol integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the relationship between assay science and throughput. The easy version of every assay doesn't scale, and the scalable version often sacrifices quality. You find the right tradeoff.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep hands-on expertise in protein production: expression (E. coli, mammalian, cell-free), purification (IMAC, SEC), and biophysical characterization (BLI and SPR at minimum). This isn't negotiable. You need to have done this work yourself, at volume.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PhD in protein biochemistry, biophysics, or structural biology, plus 3-5 years in a production or development role at a CRO, foundry, or high-throughput lab. Academic postdocs count if the work was high-throughput and production-oriented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high-throughput workflows. You're comfortable with 96-well plates and liquid handlers, not just single-column purifications. You've optimized protocols for scale, not just for one perfect result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentorship mindset. You've managed or trained junior scientists before. You enjoy teaching and get satisfaction from watching your team grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshooting instinct. When data looks wrong, your first impulse is to understand why, not to rerun the experiment and hope it works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quality-obsessed but pragmatic. You care deeply about data quality, but you also understand that production has deadlines and sometimes "good enough" is the right call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bridge between R&amp;D and production. You can speak both languages: the exploratory mindset of research and the reproducibility demands of production.</p></li></ul><h2>Details</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Lausanne, Switzerland (on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Type:</strong> Full time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We review applications on a rolling basis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/production-scientist-senior-lausanne-16629","tags":["Biology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792064438},{"slug":"laboratory-technician-lab-operations-lausanne-369229","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Laboratory Technician, Lab Operations","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our lab in Lausanne runs thousands of constructs a week through automated workcells, liquid handlers, and binding instruments. That only works if the instruments are calibrated, the buffers are made, the stock is where the system says it is, and the bench is ready when the scientists arrive. You are the person who makes sure it is.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the day-to-day upkeep of our automation and instruments, run buffer and reagent production, keep the lab clean, safe, and stocked, and lead the rollout of new inventory management and lab operations processes across the lab. This is a hands-on, in-the-lab role, working closely with our Lab Manager, the Lab Operations team, and the scientists whose experiments depend on you getting it right.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run daily and weekly calibration of our Hamilton liquid handling systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calibrate and maintain key instruments, including the Echo and pH meters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Look after the SPR system: buffer bottle changes, rinsing, and routine upkeep.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of our automated workcells and keep them clean, organized, and calibrated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare buffers, reagents, and reaction mixes according to established SOPs. Run weekly buffer production and handle ad-hoc requests from the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the rollout of new inventory management and lab operations processes across the lab, and help design and improve them as the lab scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organize fridges and storage, run inventory, and keep consumables, glassware, and bench supplies stocked so experiments never stall.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep benches and shared spaces clean, clear, and ready for work every day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage hazardous and biohazardous waste disposal (including broken glass and sharps), waste sorting, recycling, and general waste removal in line with safety regulations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the lab dishwasher and make sure clean glassware is always available.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and document scheduled deep cleans and preventive maintenance.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Laboratory apprenticeship (CFC Laborant/in), BSc in a relevant field, or an equivalent lab technician qualification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Precision in following and executing protocols and SOPs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A service mindset. You enjoy making other people's work easier.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with routine, with an eye for ways to improve it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calm and reliable in a fast-paced, high-throughput environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with lab automation or liquid handling systems (Hamilton, Echo, or similar) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with inventory or LIMS tools is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in English and French is a plus. Many of our vendors and delivery services operate in French.</p></li></ul><h2>Details</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Lausanne, Switzerland (on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Type:</strong> Full time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We review applications on a rolling basis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/laboratory-technician-lab-operations-lausanne-369229","tags":["Biology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792064438},{"slug":"bioengineer-molecular-biologist-lausanne-48490","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Bioengineer / Molecular Biologist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on research role in our biology and production team. You'll work on the science that underpins everything Adaptyv does: developing and optimizing protein expression systems, running molecular biology workflows, and pushing the boundaries of what we can produce and characterize at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We express proteins at high volume across cell-free and cell-based systems, run DNA synthesis and assembly at high throughput, and characterize binding, stability, and function using BLI, SPR, and enzymatic assays.</p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and optimize protein expression workflows - cell-free expression (PURE, lysate-based), E. coli, and potentially mammalian systems. Troubleshoot when proteins don't express, misfold, or aggregate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and execute DNA synthesis and assembly protocols: PCR, Golden Gate, Gibson. Improve yield, fidelity, and throughput.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop new assays or adapt existing ones for the platform - thermostability, developability, enzyme activity, or whatever the next customer need demands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run experiments yourself. This is not a project management role. You'll be at the bench doing molecular biology, analyzing data, and iterating on protocols.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the automation team to translate your methods into automated workflows. You develop the protocol that works; they make the robots run it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze experimental data, identify failure modes, and improve methods systematically. When 20% of constructs in a batch fail to express, you figure out why.</p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>MSc or PhD in molecular biology, biochemistry, bioengineering, or a related field.</strong> Hands-on depth matters most - years at the bench doing real molecular biology counts more than the degree title.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Practical protein expression and purification skills.</strong> You've expressed recombinant proteins and know what it takes to get them soluble, folded, and functional.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience with DNA synthesis, cloning, or assembly methods</strong> (PCR, Golden Gate, Gibson). High-throughput experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable with data analysis</strong> - you interpret chromatograms, binding curves, and expression gels without hand-holding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rigorous experimentalist.</strong> You keep detailed notes, design proper controls, and understand why reproducibility matters when you're running hundreds of experiments a month.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interested in automation.</strong> You don't need to program robots, but you should want your protocols to become automated workflows rather than staying manual forever.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Independent and resourceful.</strong> You troubleshoot using literature, first principles, and experimentation - not by waiting for someone to tell you what to try next.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Lausanne, Switzerland (on-site - this is a lab role).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/bioengineer-molecular-biologist-lausanne-48490","tags":["Biology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792064438},{"slug":"scientist-protein-expression-purification-lausanne-14943","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Scientist, Protein Expression & Purification","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll build out protein expression and purification at Adaptyv, with a focus on mammalian systems — CHO and HEK, transient and stable. This is the foundation the rest of the platform stands on: titers, quality, and turnaround here set the ceiling for everything downstream.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your job is to take expression and purification from bespoke, person-dependent protocols to a robust, automated, high-throughput product. You'll optimize and run the science hands-on, work with lab automation to scale it onto liquid handlers and automated systems, and work with the software team to track samples, capture process data, and make production observable and predictable. You'll lead the science and stay deeply hands-on.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop, optimize, and run mammalian expression hands-on (CHO/HEK, transient and stable), pushing titer, quality, and reproducibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own purification across modalities (Protein A, IEX, SEC, and related) and the quality of the proteins we ship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn expression and purification into a productized, high-throughput, automated capability with predictable turnaround.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with lab automation to scale workflows onto automated systems, and reduce manual, person-dependent steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the software team to track samples and process parameters, and make production yields and quality observable and improvable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the quality bar and troubleshoot the inevitable failures across biology, reagents, and process.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep, hands-on expertise in mammalian protein expression and purification</strong> — CHO/HEK, and the full path from construct to purified, characterized protein.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applied industry experience.</strong> You've run expression and purification in a production or industrial setting — where yield, reproducibility, and turnaround mattered at scale — not primarily in an academic research project. This is the core requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Track record of making production reliable</strong> — titer optimization, scale-up, and consistent quality, not one-off preps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder who moves fast.</strong> You want to stand up and continuously improve a production capability, not run a fixed protocol.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interdisciplinary.</strong> You collaborate naturally with automation engineers and software people, and you see automation and data as core to a modern production process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data fluency (scripting, tracking and analyzing process data) is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><h2>Details</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Lausanne, Switzerland (on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Type:</strong> Full time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/scientist-protein-expression-purification-lausanne-14943","tags":["Biology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792064438},{"slug":"qualifizierungsingenieur-gmp-compliance-projektstandort-visp-335786","company_name":"Bakerhicks","title":"Qualifizierungsingenieur (w/m/d) - GMP Compliance / Projektstandort Visp","description":"&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Für unseren Projektstandort in &lt;strong&gt;Visp&lt;/strong&gt; suchen wir einen Qualifizierungsingenieur (w/m/d) mit Eintrittstermin nach Absprache.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Deine Aufgaben&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bereitest Risikoanalysen sowie Qualifizierungen (DQ, IQ, OQ, PQ) projektgerecht vor, führst sie durch, dokumentierst und wertest sie aus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du identifizierst Ursachen, bewertest fachlich und setzt Change- sowie Abweichungsmanagement (inkl. CAPA) um – inklusive deren Nachverfolgung und Überwachung.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In der Erstellung von SOPs sowie in der Planung und Durchführung GMP-konformer Schulungen bringst Du Dein Know-how ein.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du unterstützt aktiv bei der Vorbereitung, Durchführung und Nachbereitung externer Inspektionen (Audits) im Bereich Qualifizierung.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Die Qualifizierung von Process Automation Systems (PAS) gehört ebenfalls zu Deinem Verantwortungsbereich.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;liquidDesignProfilePublication&quot; class=&quot;liquid-design-box&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Dein Profil&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du hast ein Studium in Biotechnologie, Chemieingenieurwesen, Pharma-/Medizintechnik oder eine vergleichbare Ausbildung sowie mindestens 5 Jahre Erfahrung im Bereich CQV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualifizierungsprozesse, Projektmanagement und Projektverantwortung sind Dir vertraut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du arbeitest qualitätsorientiert, selbstständig und bringst ein hohes Maß an Eigeninitiative mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mit Deinen sehr guten analytischen Fähigkeiten und Deiner strukturierten Arbeitsweise überzeugst Du im Projektalltag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bist kommunikationsstark in Deutsch und Englisch, moderierst sicher und bist projektbezogen im In- und Ausland reisebereit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-end=&quot;15&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Über BakerHicks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;17&quot; data-end=&quot;251&quot;&gt;Seit 1957 sind wir Vorreiter in den Bereichen Design, Engineering und Projektmanagement. Von der Beratung bis hin zum Bau und der Compliance unterstützen unsere multidisziplinären Design- und Ingenieurteams Unternehmen auf der ganzen Welt dabei, ihre Projekte auf die effizienteste, kostengünstigste und nachhaltigste Weise zu realisieren.&lt;/p&gt;
